{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/serve.cljc | sed -n '1,700p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.repl.serve\n     2\t  \"The server side of the DaoStream Yin REPL, over the request-and-response\n     3\t   service of docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md section 5.\n     4\t\n     5\t   `serve!` composes an endpoint and returns immediately with one explicit\n     6\t   value: the shared `\\\"yin.repl/requests\\\"` and `\\\"yin.repl/answers\\\"`\n     7\t   media a `dao.stream.remote` mirror table names, the boundary control\n     8\t   medium, the bounded acceptance handoff pool, the composition-owned\n     9\t   lifecycle medium with its already-minted cursor, and the one shared\n    10\t   shell every request evaluates against (D4).  Binding a listener is host\n    11\t   policy, injected through `yin.repl.host`; every fact about it —\n    12\t   `:bind-succeeded`, `:bind-failed`, `:upgrade-failed`, `:listener-error`,\n    13\t   `:stopped` — arrives as plain data on the lifecycle medium, and no host\n    14\t   error object crosses the boundary.\n    15\t\n    16\t   `step` is the single server driver: it observes lifecycle, drives\n    17\t   `dao.stream.ws-project/accept-step!` (which itself adopts every accepted\n    18\t   connection's own private wire channel and runs `dao.stream.remote`'s\n    19\t   mirror over it, answering every `:dao.stream/cursor`, `/next`,\n    20\t   `/append!`, and `/descriptor` a connected client's reflections ask), and\n    21\t   advances the one shared requests/answers pair against a single serially\n    22\t   threaded REPL state.  It never loops on `blocked`, never waits, and\n    23\t   never schedules itself.  There is no per-attachment session pool here\n    24\t   any more: correlation is by the self-minted random id every request and\n    25\t   answer value carries (`dao.stream.rpc`), not by which WebSocket\n    26\t   connection carried it, so one shared pair serves every connected client\n    27\t   exactly as the service convention's toy peer S does.\"\n    28\t  (:require [dao.data :as data]\n    29\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    30\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n    31\t            [dao.stream.rpc :as rpc]\n    32\t            [dao.stream.ws :as ws]\n    33\t            [dao.stream.ws-project :as ws-project]\n    34\t            [yin.repl.connect :as connect]\n    35\t            [yin.repl :as repl]\n    36\t            [yin.repl.host.common :as host-common]))\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\t;; =============================================================================\n    40\t;; Composition constants\n    41\t;; =============================================================================\n    42\t\n    43\t(def control-capacity 1024)\n    44\t(def request-capacity 8192)\n    45\t(def lifecycle-capacity 256)\n    46\t(def default-slot-count 8)\n    47\t(def default-bind-host \"127.0.0.1\")\n    48\t(def lifecycle-budget 64)\n    49\t(def request-budget 64)\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t(def ^:private diagnostic-bounds\n    53\t  \"Bound on operator-facing diagnostic text built from unbounded internal\n    54\t   state (unvalidated bind config, host-reported lifecycle values).\"\n    55\t  {:depth 3 :items 8 :chars 200})\n    56\t\n    57\t\n    58\t(def eval-operation :op/eval)\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\t(def incomplete-input-code\n    62\t  \"This server's refusal of a well-formed request whose source is an unbalanced\n    63\t   form.  The envelope owner's malformed-request code would misreport it as a\n    64\t   codec defect.\"\n    65\t  :yin.repl.serve/incomplete-input)\n    66\t\n    67\t\n    68\t(def wildcard-hosts #{\"0.0.0.0\" \"::\" \"[::]\" \"*\"})\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t(def event-key :yin.repl.endpoint/event)\n    72\t(def value-key :yin.repl.endpoint/value)\n    73\t\n    74\t\n    75\t(def event-kinds\n    76\t  \"The fixed lifecycle event set.  An unknown kind is surfaced as a diagnostic\n    77\t   rather than silently ignored or trusted.\"\n    78\t  #{:bind-succeeded :bind-failed :upgrade-failed :listener-error :stopped})\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\t(def outbox-event-key :yin.repl.serve/event)\n    82\t(def text-key :yin.repl.serve/text)\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\t(def portable-admission\n    86\t  {:retention :evict-oldest :capacity control-capacity :value-domain :portable-values})\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t(def request-admission\n    90\t  {:retention :evict-oldest :capacity request-capacity :value-domain :portable-values})\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\t(def handoff-admission\n    94\t  {:retention :evict-oldest :capacity 1 :value-domain :host-values})\n    95\t\n    96\t\n    97\t;; =============================================================================\n    98\t;; Small composition helpers\n    99\t;; =============================================================================\n   100\t\n   101\t(defn- buffer\n   102\t  [capacity]\n   103\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n   104\t    (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n   105\t                   ring/capacity-key capacity})))\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\t(defn- mint\n   109\t  [handle anchor]\n   110\t  (let [result (stream/cursor handle anchor)]\n   111\t    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n   112\t      (:dao.stream/cursor result))))\n   113\t\n   114\t\n   115\t(defn- writer-target\n   116\t  [handle]\n   117\t  {:dao.stream/handle handle :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}})\n   118\t\n   119\t\n   120\t(defn- publish\n   121\t  [endpoint kind text]\n   122\t  (update endpoint :outbox conj {outbox-event-key kind text-key text}))\n   123\t\n   124\t\n   125\t(defn take-outbox\n   126\t  \"Return `[entries next-endpoint]`, clearing the publication outbox once.\"\n   127\t  [endpoint]\n   128\t  [(:outbox endpoint) (assoc endpoint :outbox [])])\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\t(defn- deposit-fn\n   132\t  [lifecycle]\n   133\t  (fn deposit!\n   134\t    [kind value]\n   135\t    (stream/append! lifecycle {event-key kind value-key value})))\n   136\t\n   137\t\n   138\t;; =============================================================================\n   139\t;; serve!\n   140\t;; =============================================================================\n   141\t\n   142\t(defn- make-slots\n   143\t  [n]\n   144\t  (mapv (fn [_]\n   145\t          (let [offer (buffer 1)\n   146\t                ack (buffer 1)]\n   147\t            {:offer offer :ack ack\n   148\t             :offer-cursor (mint offer stream/anchor-newest)\n   149\t             :ack-cursor (mint ack stream/anchor-newest)}))\n   150\t        (range n)))\n   151\t\n   152\t\n   153\t(defn- endpoint-slots\n   154\t  [slots]\n   155\t  (mapv (fn [slot]\n   156\t          {:offer (writer-target (:offer slot))\n   157\t           :offer-admission handoff-admission\n   158\t           :ack (writer-target (:ack slot))\n   159\t           :ack-admission handoff-admission\n   160\t           :ack-cursor (:ack-cursor slot)})\n   161\t        slots))\n   162\t\n   163\t\n   164\t(defn- serving-slots\n   165\t  [slots]\n   166\t  (mapv (fn [slot]\n   167\t          {:offer-reader (:offer slot)\n   168\t           :offer-cursor (:offer-cursor slot)\n   169\t           :ack-writer (writer-target (:ack slot))})\n   170\t        slots))\n   171\t\n   172\t\n   173\t(defn- make-media\n   174\t  \"One request medium per accepted attachment, capacity 8192, with its\n   175\t   cursor minted before the acknowledgement is deposited, plus the fresh\n   176\t   channel ring `dao.stream.ws-project/accept-step!` projects deposited\n   177\t   payload onto and mirror-steps against.  One client's eviction pressure\n   178\t   therefore cannot create another client's request gap.\"\n   179\t  [_offer]\n   180\t  (let [traffic (buffer request-capacity)]\n   181\t    {:traffic (writer-target traffic)\n   182\t     :admission request-admission\n   183\t     :reader traffic\n   184\t     :cursor (mint traffic stream/anchor-newest)\n   185\t     :ring (buffer request-capacity)}))\n   186\t\n   187\t\n   188\t(defn- inert\n   189\t  \"An endpoint value that owns its media and reports why it never bound.\"\n   190\t  [base kind value text]\n   191\t  (let [deposit! (deposit-fn (:lifecycle base))]\n   192\t    (deposit! kind value)\n   193\t    (assoc base :status :failed :bind-note text)))\n   194\t\n   195\t\n   196\t(defn serve!\n   197\t  \"Compose a REPL endpoint and return immediately.\n   198\t\n   199\t   Every medium and every cursor exists before any binding is attempted:\n   200\t   the shared requests and answers media, the boundary control medium,\n   201\t   each handoff slot's offer and acknowledgement media, and the lifecycle\n   202\t   medium.  The returned value is the whole of the endpoint's observable\n   203\t   state; `step` is the only thing that changes it.\"\n   204\t  [{:keys [bind-host bind-port advertised-host advertised-port path slots host\n   205\t           repl identity expiry-ms]\n   206\t    :or {bind-host default-bind-host slots default-slot-count}}]\n   207\t  (let [path (connect/repl-target (or path \"\"))\n   208\t        control (buffer control-capacity)\n   209\t        lifecycle (buffer lifecycle-capacity)\n   210\t        lifecycle-cursor (mint lifecycle stream/anchor-newest)\n   211\t        control-cursor (mint control stream/anchor-newest)\n   212\t        pool (make-slots (max 1 slots))\n   213\t        advertised-host (or advertised-host\n   214\t                            (when-not (contains? wildcard-hosts bind-host) bind-host))\n   215\t        advertised-port (or advertised-port bind-port)\n   216\t        descriptor {:dao.stream/type ws/transport-type\n   217\t                    :dao.stream/identity (or identity connect/service-identity)\n   218\t                    :ws/host (str advertised-host)\n   219\t                    :ws/port (if (integer? advertised-port) advertised-port 0)\n   220\t                    :ws/path path}\n   221\t        requests (buffer request-capacity)\n   222\t        answers (buffer request-capacity)\n   223\t        requests-cursor (mint requests stream/anchor-oldest)\n   224\t        table {connect/requests-identity {:handle requests :surface #{:writer}}\n   225\t               connect/answers-identity {:handle answers :surface #{:reader}}}\n   226\t        base {:control control\n   227\t              :control-cursor control-cursor\n   228\t              :lifecycle lifecycle\n   229\t              :lifecycle-cursor lifecycle-cursor\n   230\t              :lifecycle-ledger :untried\n   231\t              :slots pool\n   232\t              :path path\n   233\t              :descriptor descriptor\n   234\t              :bind-host bind-host\n   235\t              :bind-port bind-port\n   236\t              :resolution nil\n   237\t              :requests requests\n   238\t              :answers answers\n   239\t              :requests-cursor requests-cursor\n   240\t              :pending-answer nil\n   241\t              :pending-successor nil\n   242\t              :host host\n   243\t              :resources (atom nil)\n   244\t              :repl (or repl (repl/create-state))\n   245\t              :status :new\n   246\t              :stop-initiated? false\n   247\t              :step-moved? false\n   248\t              :outbox []}]\n   249\t    (cond\n   250\t      (nil? advertised-host)\n   251\t      (inert base :bind-failed\n   252\t             {:code :yin.repl.endpoint/advertised-host-required\n   253\t              :message \"a wildcard bind requires an explicit advertised host\"}\n   254\t             (str \"--host \" bind-host \" needs an explicit advertised host\"))\n   255\t\n   256\t      ;; Known limit of this slice, stated rather than hidden behind the\n   257\t      ;; descriptor gate: the advertised descriptor is fixed at `serve!`, so a\n   258\t      ;; bind to port zero has no advertised port to name.  Serving an\n   259\t      ;; ephemeral port means constructing the endpoint after `:bind-succeeded`,\n   260\t      ;; which is a design change to the R4 composition, not a local fix.\n   261\t      (= 0 advertised-port)\n   262\t      (inert base :bind-failed\n   263\t             {:code :yin.repl.endpoint/ephemeral-port-unsupported\n   264\t              :message (str \"an ephemeral bind has no advertised port until it \"\n   265\t                            \"binds, and this slice fixes the descriptor at serve!\")}\n   266\t             \"--port 0 needs an explicit advertised port in this slice\")\n   267\t\n   268\t      (not (ws/descriptor? descriptor))\n   269\t      (inert base :bind-failed\n   270\t             {:code :yin.repl.endpoint/invalid-descriptor\n   271\t              :message \"bind/advertised configuration does not name a servable stream\"}\n   272\t             (str \"cannot serve \" (pr-str (data/summarize path diagnostic-bounds))\n   273\t                  \" on port \" (pr-str (data/summarize bind-port diagnostic-bounds))))\n   274\t\n   275\t      (not (host-common/binder? host))\n   276\t      (inert base :bind-failed\n   277\t             {:code host-common/missing-code :message host-common/missing-text}\n   278\t             (host-common/missing-message \"--port is not served\"))\n   279\t\n   280\t      :else\n   281\t      (let [ws-endpoint (ws/make-endpoint {:served {path descriptor}\n   282\t                                           :control (writer-target control)\n   283\t                                           :control-admission portable-admission\n   284\t                                           :slots (endpoint-slots pool)\n   285\t                                           :expiry-ms expiry-ms})\n   286\t            deposit! (deposit-fn lifecycle)\n   287\t            resources (:resources base)\n   288\t            acceptor (ws-project/make-acceptor\n   289\t                       {:endpoint ws-endpoint\n   290\t                        :slots (serving-slots pool)\n   291\t                        :table table\n   292\t                        :make-media make-media})\n   293\t            bind-result\n   294\t            (try\n   295\t              (let [bound ((:bind! host)\n   296\t                           {:endpoint ws-endpoint\n   297\t                            :bind-host bind-host\n   298\t                            :bind-port bind-port\n   299\t                            :path path\n   300\t                            ;; Exactly the 3-arity `yin.repl.host/websocket`\n   301\t                            ;; documents.  A clock-omitting arity would let\n   302\t                            ;; host glue stamp a pending acceptance with\n   303\t                            ;; nil and silently disable expiry; the host\n   304\t                            ;; owns the reading, so it must supply it.\n   305\t                            :accept! (fn accept!\n   306\t                                       [request-path socket now]\n   307\t                                       (ws/accept-connection! ws-endpoint\n   308\t                                                              request-path\n   309\t                                                              socket now))\n   310\t                            :deposit! deposit!})]\n   311\t                (reset! resources bound)\n   312\t                {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})\n   313\t              (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   314\t                ;; A synchronous host bind failure is classified and\n   315\t                ;; deposited here; no host error object crosses over.\n   316\t                (deposit! :bind-failed\n   317\t                          {:code :yin.repl.endpoint/bind-threw\n   318\t                           :message \"the host listener failed to bind\"})\n   319\t                {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error}))\n   320\t            endpoint (assoc base\n   321\t                            :ws-endpoint ws-endpoint\n   322\t                            :acceptor acceptor\n   323\t                            :deposit! deposit!\n   324\t                            :resolution {path descriptor}\n   325\t                            :status (if (= :dao.stream/ok\n   326\t                                          (:dao.stream/outcome bind-result))\n   327\t                                     :starting :failed))]\n   328\t        endpoint))))\n   329\t\n   330\t\n   331\t(defn url\n   332\t  \"The descriptor as an operator would type it into `(connect …)`.\"\n   333\t  [endpoint]\n   334\t  (let [d (:descriptor endpoint)]\n   335\t    (str connect/url-prefix connect/ws-scheme (:ws/host d) \":\" (:ws/port d) (:ws/path d))))\n   336\t\n   337\t\n   338\t;; =============================================================================\n   339\t;; Lifecycle observation\n   340\t;; =============================================================================\n   341\t\n   342\t(defn- lifecycle-transition\n   343\t  [endpoint kind value]\n   344\t  (case kind\n   345\t    :bind-succeeded\n   346\t    (-> endpoint\n   347\t        (assoc :status (if (= :stopping (:status endpoint)) :stopping :running))\n   348\t        (publish :yin.repl.serve/notice\n   349\t                 (str \"Serving \" (url endpoint)\n   350\t                      (when (map? value)\n   351\t                        (str \" (bound \" (pr-str (data/summarize value diagnostic-bounds)) \")\")))))\n   352\t\n   353\t    :bind-failed\n   354\t    (-> endpoint\n   355\t        (assoc :status :failed)\n   356\t        (publish :yin.repl.serve/notice\n   357\t                 (str \";; endpoint bind failed: \"\n   358\t                      (pr-str (data/summarize value diagnostic-bounds)))))\n   359\t\n   360\t    :upgrade-failed\n   361\t    (publish endpoint :yin.repl.serve/notice\n   362\t             (str \";; upgrade refused: \" (pr-str (data/summarize value diagnostic-bounds))))\n   363\t\n   364\t    :listener-error\n   365\t    (publish endpoint :yin.repl.serve/notice\n   366\t             (str \";; listener error: \" (pr-str (data/summarize value diagnostic-bounds))))\n   367\t\n   368\t    :stopped\n   369\t    (-> endpoint\n   370\t        (assoc :status :stopped :resolution nil)\n   371\t        (publish :yin.repl.serve/notice\n   372\t                 (str \"Endpoint stopped: \" (pr-str (data/summarize value diagnostic-bounds)))))\n   373\t\n   374\t    (publish endpoint :yin.repl.serve/diagnostic\n   375\t             (str \";; unknown endpoint event \" (pr-str kind)))))\n   376\t\n   377\t\n   378\t(declare stop!)\n   379\t\n   380\t\n   381\t(defn- drain-lifecycle\n   382\t  \"Read the lifecycle medium, total over every `next` outcome.  A gap is a fatal\n   383\t   endpoint-observability failure and triggers shutdown, per R4.\"\n   384\t  [endpoint]\n   385\t  (loop [remaining lifecycle-budget\n   386\t         endpoint endpoint]\n   387\t    (if (or (zero? remaining) (nil? (:lifecycle-cursor endpoint)))\n   388\t      endpoint\n   389\t      (let [result (stream/next (:lifecycle endpoint) (:lifecycle-cursor endpoint))\n   390\t            outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)]\n   391\t        (case outcome\n   392\t          :dao.stream/ok\n   393\t          (let [envelope (:dao.stream/value result)\n   394\t                kind (get envelope event-key)\n   395\t                endpoint (assoc endpoint\n   396\t                                :lifecycle-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor result)\n   397\t                                :lifecycle-ledger outcome)]\n   398\t            (recur (dec remaining)\n   399\t                   (lifecycle-transition endpoint\n   400\t                                         (when (contains? event-kinds kind) kind)\n   401\t                                         (get envelope value-key))))\n   402\t\n   403\t          :dao.stream/gap\n   404\t          (-> endpoint\n   405\t              (assoc :lifecycle-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor result)\n   406\t                     :lifecycle-ledger outcome)\n   407\t              (publish :yin.repl.serve/notice\n   408\t                       \";; endpoint lifecycle lost: observability failed, stopping\")\n   409\t              stop!)\n   410\t\n   411\t          :dao.stream/blocked\n   412\t          (assoc endpoint :lifecycle-ledger outcome)\n   413\t\n   414\t          (-> endpoint\n   415\t              (assoc :lifecycle-ledger outcome)\n   416\t              (publish :yin.repl.serve/notice\n   417\t                       (str \";; endpoint lifecycle \" (name outcome)))))))))\n   418\t\n   419\t\n   420\t;; =============================================================================\n   421\t;; Requests\n   422\t;; =============================================================================\n   423\t\n   424\t(defn- evaluate\n   425\t  \"Answer one validated request against the one shared shell, serially.\"\n   426\t  [repl request]\n   427\t  (let [id (rpc/request-id request)]\n   428\t    (cond\n   429\t      (not= eval-operation (rpc/request-op request))\n   430\t      [repl (rpc/error-answer id :yin.repl.serve/unknown-operation\n   431\t                              \"This endpoint answers :op/eval only; it does not proxy\")]\n   432\t\n   433\t      (not (string? (first (rpc/request-args request))))\n   434\t      [repl (rpc/error-answer id :yin.repl.serve/invalid-arguments\n   435\t                              \"An :op/eval request carries one source string\")]\n   436\t\n   437\t      :else\n   438\t      (try\n   439\t        (let [[repl' text] (repl/eval-input repl (first (rpc/request-args request)))]\n   440\t          (if (:pending-input repl')\n   441\t            ;; Line continuation is a terminal concern.  One shared shell means\n   442\t            ;; an unbalanced request would otherwise prefix the *next*\n   443\t            ;; caller's source, so the fragment is refused and dropped here\n   444\t            ;; rather than retained across a caller boundary.  The envelope\n   445\t            ;; was well formed, so the refusal is this server's decision and\n   446\t            ;; carries this server's code: a client can tell it from a codec\n   447\t            ;; defect.\n   448\t            [(assoc repl' :pending-input nil)\n   449\t             (rpc/error-answer id incomplete-input-code\n   450\t                               \"Incomplete input: a request carries one complete form\")]\n   451\t            [repl' (rpc/success-answer id text)]))\n   452\t        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   453\t          [repl (rpc/error-answer id :yin.repl.serve/handler-error \"Handler failed\")])))))\n   454\t\n   455\t\n   456\t(defn- deliver-answer\n   457\t  \"Append one retained answer, advancing the requests cursor only when the\n   458\t   append is accepted.  `full` retries the identical answer on a later step\n   459\t   without re-running the handler.\"\n   460\t  [endpoint]\n   461\t  (let [result (stream/append! (:answers endpoint) (:pending-answer endpoint))\n   462\t        outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)]\n   463\t    (case outcome\n   464\t      :dao.stream/ok\n   465\t      (assoc endpoint\n   466\t             :requests-cursor (:pending-successor endpoint)\n   467\t             :pending-answer nil\n   468\t             :pending-successor nil)\n   469\t\n   470\t      :dao.stream/full\n   471\t      endpoint\n   472\t\n   473\t      (-> endpoint\n   474\t          (assoc :requests-cursor (:pending-successor endpoint)\n   475\t                 :pending-answer nil\n   476\t                 :pending-successor nil)\n   477\t          (publish :yin.repl.serve/notice\n   478\t                   (str \";; answer undeliverable: \" (name outcome)))))))\n   479\t\n   480\t\n   481\t(defn- advance-requests\n   482\t  \"One bounded sweep of the shared requests/answers pair: a pending answer\n   483\t   is retried first (its retry runs on the host's cadence, gated on\n   484\t   nothing), then at most `request-budget` further request/answer cycles.\n   485\t   Correlation is by the self-minted random id every request and answer\n   486\t   carries (`dao.stream.rpc`), never by which connection carried it -- the\n   487\t   mirror already answered every wire-protocol question a reflection\n   488\t   asked; this is the interpreter over the local requests/answers ends the\n   489\t   service convention names.\"\n   490\t  [endpoint]\n   491\t  (loop [remaining request-budget\n   492\t         endpoint endpoint]\n   493\t    (cond\n   494\t      (zero? remaining) endpoint\n   495\t\n   496\t      (:pending-answer endpoint)\n   497\t      (let [endpoint (deliver-answer endpoint)]\n   498\t        (if (:pending-answer endpoint)\n   499\t          endpoint\n   500\t          (recur (dec remaining) endpoint)))\n   501\t\n   502\t      :else\n   503\t      (let [result (stream/next (:requests endpoint) (:requests-cursor endpoint))\n   504\t            outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)]\n   505\t        (case outcome\n   506\t          :dao.stream/ok\n   507\t          (let [request (:dao.stream/value result)\n   508\t                successor (:dao.stream/cursor result)]\n   509\t            (cond\n   510\t              (rpc/request-value? request)\n   511\t              (let [[repl' answer] (evaluate (:repl endpoint) request)]\n   512\t                (recur remaining\n   513\t                       (assoc endpoint\n   514\t                              :repl repl'\n   515\t                              :pending-answer answer\n   516\t                              :pending-successor successor)))\n   517\t\n   518\t              ;; Correlatable but malformed: an error answer at least tells\n   519\t              ;; the caller their own request failed, distinct from silence.\n   520\t              (and (map? request) (rpc/safe-id? (:dao.stream.rpc/id request)))\n   521\t              (recur remaining\n   522\t                     (assoc endpoint\n   523\t                            :pending-answer\n   524\t                            (rpc/error-answer (:dao.stream.rpc/id request)\n   525\t                                             :yin.repl.serve/malformed-request\n   526\t                                             \"Malformed request envelope\")\n   527\t                            :pending-successor successor))\n   528\t\n   529\t              :else\n   530\t              (recur (dec remaining)\n   531\t                     (-> endpoint\n   532\t                         (assoc :requests-cursor successor)\n   533\t                         (publish :yin.repl.serve/diagnostic\n   534\t                                  \";; malformed request dropped\")))))\n   535\t\n   536\t          :dao.stream/blocked endpoint\n   537\t\n   538\t          :dao.stream/gap\n   539\t          (recur (dec remaining)\n   540\t                 (-> endpoint\n   541\t                     (assoc :requests-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor result))\n   542\t                     (publish :yin.repl.serve/notice\n   543\t                              \";; requests lost; resuming at the recovery cursor\")))\n   544\t\n   545\t          (publish endpoint :yin.repl.serve/notice\n   546\t                   (str \";; requests \" (name outcome))))))))\n   547\t\n   548\t\n   549\t;; =============================================================================\n   550\t;; Stop\n   551\t;; =============================================================================\n   552\t\n   553\t(defn stopped?\n   554\t  \"True when nothing more is owed to this endpoint's shutdown: it reported\n   555\t   `:stopped`, or it never composed an acceptor at all.\n   556\t\n   557\t   A refused bind configuration or a missing host package leaves an endpoint\n   558\t   that owns its media and its reason and nothing else.  No host close\n   559\t   completion exists to deposit `:stopped` for it, so a shutdown that waited for\n   560\t   one would spend its whole budget and then report a timeout for a listener\n   561\t   that never bound.\"\n   562\t  [endpoint]\n   563\t  (or (nil? endpoint)\n   564\t      (= :stopped (:status endpoint))\n   565\t      (nil? (:acceptor endpoint))))\n   566\t\n   567\t\n   568\t(defn stop!\n   569\t  \"Initiate stop, claiming nothing about completion.\n   570\t\n   571\t   Closing the shared requests and answers media is what makes a connected\n   572\t   client observe `:dao.stream/end` -- the bare source outcome the mirror\n   573\t   relays verbatim -- on its next read, translated to `:dao.stream.apply/\n   574\t   ended`: a permanent conclusion, never a reattachable detach.  Every\n   575\t   accepted session's own socket closes later, in `finish-stop`, once this\n   576\t   step's mirror pass has had the chance to deliver that answer over the\n   577\t   wire; closing it here would race that delivery.  Only the host close\n   578\t   completion deposits `:stopped`, and only `step` consuming it marks the\n   579\t   stop complete and releases the resolution-table entry.\n   580\t\n   581\t   An endpoint with no acceptor is left exactly as it is: it holds no\n   582\t   listener and no attachment, so there is nothing to initiate, and marking it\n   583\t   `:stopping` would both claim a stop nobody can complete and erase the status\n   584\t   that says why it never started.\"\n   585\t  [endpoint]\n   586\t  (if (or (contains? #{:stopping :stopped} (:status endpoint))\n   587\t          (nil? (:acceptor endpoint)))\n   588\t    endpoint\n   589\t    (do\n   590\t      (stream/close! (:answers endpoint))\n   591\t      (stream/close! (:requests endpoint))\n   592\t      (assoc endpoint :status :stopping))))\n   593\t\n   594\t\n   595\t(def stop-grace-ms\n   596\t  \"How long, in the caller's clock domain, `finish-stop` waits after\n   597\t   `stop!` closed the shared requests/answers media before it closes any\n   598\t   accepted session's socket.  Closing the socket too soon would race the\n   599\t   wire answer a client's outstanding read of the now-ended media is\n   600\t   owed: that read answers with the media's own `:dao.stream/end`, and\n   601\t   the client must see that -- `:ended`, never reattachable -- before its\n   602\t   socket also reports `:ws/closed`, which alone would read as a\n   603\t   reattachable detach.  A fixed step count cannot bound this: it says\n   604\t   nothing about the client's own independent poll cadence or the network\n   605\t   round trip its read takes.\"\n   606\t  500)\n   607\t\n   608\t\n   609\t(defn- finish-stop*\n   610\t  [endpoint]\n   611\t  (if (:stop-initiated? endpoint)\n   612\t    endpoint\n   613\t    (let [endpoint (assoc endpoint :stop-initiated? true)\n   614\t          endpoint (do (doseq [[_ session] (ws-project/sessions (:acceptor endpoint))]\n   615\t                         (stream/close! (:handle session)))\n   616\t                       endpoint)\n   617\t          bound @(:resources endpoint)\n   618\t          result\n   619\t          (if bound\n   620\t            (try\n   621\t              ((:unbind! (:host endpoint)) bound (:deposit! endpoint))\n   622\t              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}\n   623\t              (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   624\t                (let [reason {:code :yin.repl.endpoint/unbind-threw\n   625\t                              :message \"the host listener failed to release\"}]\n   626\t                  ((:deposit! endpoint) :listener-error reason)\n   627\t                  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n   628\t                   :dao.stream/diagnostic reason})))\n   629\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n   630\t             :dao.stream/diagnostic\n   631\t             {:code :yin.repl.endpoint/never-bound\n   632\t              :message \"the host listener never returned a resource\"}})]\n   633\t      (if (= :dao.stream/transport-error (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n   634\t        ;; A synchronous release failure has no later host completion to\n   635\t        ;; observe.  The composition owns that fact and resolves locally,\n   636\t        ;; retaining the structured reason in the ordinary notice stream.\n   637\t        (-> endpoint\n   638\t            (assoc :status :stopped :resolution nil)\n   639\t            (publish :yin.repl.serve/notice\n   640\t                     (str \"Endpoint stopped without host completion: \"\n   641\t                          (pr-str (data/summarize (:dao.stream/diagnostic result)\n   642\t                                                  diagnostic-bounds)))))\n   643\t        endpoint))))\n   644\t\n   645\t\n   646\t(defn- finish-stop\n   647\t  [endpoint now]\n   648\t  (cond\n   649\t    (not= :stopping (:status endpoint)) endpoint\n   650\t    (nil? (:acceptor endpoint)) endpoint\n   651\t\n   652\t    ;; Nothing to wait for: skip the grace period entirely rather than\n   653\t    ;; delay a stop with no accepted session to deliver anything to.\n   654\t    (empty? (ws-project/sessions (:acceptor endpoint))) (finish-stop* endpoint)\n   655\t\n   656\t    ;; Real elapsed time, not a step count: a fixed number of this\n   657\t    ;; endpoint's own ticks says nothing about whether a client's\n   658\t    ;; independent poll cadence -- and the network round trip its own\n   659\t    ;; read takes -- has actually had the chance to run in that time.\n   660\t    (nil? (:stop-requested-at endpoint))\n   661\t    (assoc endpoint :stop-requested-at now)\n   662\t\n   663\t    (< (- now (:stop-requested-at endpoint)) stop-grace-ms)\n   664\t    endpoint\n   665\t\n   666\t    :else\n   667\t    (finish-stop* endpoint)))\n   668\t\n   669\t\n   670\t;; =============================================================================\n   671\t;; The driver step\n   672\t;; =============================================================================\n   673\t\n   674\t(defn step\n   675\t  \"Advance the endpoint once at `now`, returning the next endpoint value.\n   676\t\n   677\t   Ordering is intentional: lifecycle first, so a bind result is known before\n   678\t   anything claims to be serving; then the accepting composition's own\n   679\t   transport/offer/mirror step; then one bounded sweep of the shared\n   680\t   requests/answers pair against the single shared REPL state.\"\n   681\t  [endpoint now]\n   682\t  (if-not endpoint\n   683\t    endpoint\n   684\t    (let [outbox-before (count (:outbox endpoint))\n   685\t          endpoint (drain-lifecycle endpoint)]\n   686\t      (if-not (:acceptor endpoint)\n   687\t        ;; An endpoint that never composed an acceptor -- a refused bind\n   688\t        ;; configuration or a missing host package -- still owns and reports\n   689\t        ;; its lifecycle medium; it simply has no requests to advance.\n   690\t        endpoint\n   691\t        (let [before (set (keys (ws-project/sessions (:acceptor endpoint))))\n   692\t              _ (ws-project/accept-step! (:acceptor endpoint) now)\n   693\t              departed (remove (ws-project/sessions (:acceptor endpoint)) before)\n   694\t              endpoint (reduce (fn [endpoint attachment]\n   695\t                                 (publish endpoint :yin.repl.serve/notice\n   696\t                                          (str \";; attachment \" attachment \" left\")))\n   697\t                               endpoint departed)\n   698\t              cursor-before (:requests-cursor endpoint)\n   699\t              endpoint (advance-requests endpoint)]\n   700\t          (-> endpoint\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/serve.cljc | sed -n '700,735p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/connect.cljc | sed -n '1,610p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/serve.cljc | sed -n '700,735p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/connect.cljc | sed -n '1,610p'\"","aggregated_output":"   700\t          (-> endpoint\n   701\t              (assoc :step-moved?\n   702\t                     (boolean (or (some? (:pending-answer endpoint))\n   703\t                                 (not= cursor-before (:requests-cursor endpoint))\n   704\t                                 (> (count (:outbox endpoint)) outbox-before))))\n   705\t              (finish-stop now)))))))\n   706\t\n   707\t\n   708\t(defn moved?\n   709\t  \"True when the last `step` moved something a caller's cadence must not\n   710\t   sleep through: a notice was published, or a computed answer still owes\n   711\t   an append, which must never wait out a backoff ceiling.\"\n   712\t  [endpoint]\n   713\t  (boolean (or (:step-moved? endpoint) (:pending-answer endpoint))))\n   714\t\n   715\t\n   716\t(defn summary\n   717\t  \"A serializable summary of endpoint state, for `(repl-state)` and tests.\"\n   718\t  [endpoint]\n   719\t  (when endpoint\n   720\t    {:status (:status endpoint)\n   721\t     :url (url endpoint)\n   722\t     :path (:path endpoint)\n   723\t     :identity (:dao.stream/identity (:descriptor endpoint))\n   724\t     :serving? (some? (:resolution endpoint))\n   725\t     :sessions (if (:acceptor endpoint)\n   726\t                (vec (sort (keys (ws-project/sessions (:acceptor endpoint)))))\n   727\t                [])\n   728\t     :lifecycle {:cursor (:lifecycle-cursor endpoint)\n   729\t                 :last-outcome (:lifecycle-ledger endpoint)}}))\n     1\t(ns yin.repl.connect\n     2\t  \"The client side of the DaoStream Yin REPL, over the request-and-response\n     3\t   service of docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md section 5.\n     4\t\n     5\t   One connection is one explicit value.  `open` canonicalizes the URL to the\n     6\t   request-target form `dao.stream.ws.md` defines, dials one WebSocket\n     7\t   channel through `dao.stream.ws-project`, and attaches two\n     8\t   `dao.stream.remote` reflections over it -- one of `\\\"yin.repl/requests\\\"`\n     9\t   (this end writes), one of `\\\"yin.repl/answers\\\"` (this end reads) -- both\n    10\t   sharing the one link the dial establishes.  `attach!` over\n    11\t   `dao.stream.remote` answers ok at once: that is the contract's deferred\n    12\t   remote confirmation, not a promise that the server has resolved anything,\n    13\t   so a connection is reported `:established` immediately rather than\n    14\t   waiting on an asynchronous transport event.\n    15\t\n    16\t   The dial is reusable across reconnects: `close!` closes the underlying\n    17\t   channel handle, and reattaching redials the same `attach!` and repeats\n    18\t   both reflection attaches, then `rpc/rebind`s the retained RPC client onto\n    19\t   the fresh pair -- which keeps its response cursor and its outstanding\n    20\t   bookkeeping, exactly as before.  Terminal status\n    21\t   (`:detached`/`:ended`/`:not-found`/`:transport-error`) is observed from\n    22\t   the RPC client's own `:terminal`, translated by `dao.stream.rpc`'s\n    23\t   reflection-read translation; `observe-terminal` turns that into the one\n    24\t   connection notice each terminal reason publishes exactly once.\"\n    25\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n    26\t            [dao.data :as data]\n    27\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    28\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n    29\t            [dao.stream.rpc :as rpc]\n    30\t            [dao.stream.ws :as ws]\n    31\t            [dao.stream.ws-project :as ws-project]\n    32\t            [yin.repl.host.common :as host-common]))\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t;; =============================================================================\n    36\t;; Composition constants\n    37\t;; =============================================================================\n    38\t\n    39\t(def traffic-capacity\n    40\t  \"Declared capacity of the boundary's one traffic medium, in elements.  It is\n    41\t   reused across reconnects because a client boundary has at most one active\n    42\t   attachment at a time.\"\n    43\t  8192)\n    44\t\n    45\t\n    46\t(def traffic-admission\n    47\t  {:retention :evict-oldest\n    48\t   :capacity traffic-capacity\n    49\t   :value-domain :portable-values})\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t(def url-prefix \"daostream:\")\n    53\t(def ws-scheme \"ws://\")\n    54\t(def secure-scheme \"wss://\")\n    55\t(def default-port 8080)\n    56\t\n    57\t\n    58\t(def repl-path\n    59\t  \"The path an empty URL path means for this REPL (D3).  An explicit `/`\n    60\t   remains `/`; only an absent path becomes the served REPL stream.\"\n    61\t  \"/repl\")\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\t(def service-identity\n    65\t  \"The logical identity of the WebSocket channel a REPL endpoint serves.  A\n    66\t   descriptor names a served stream, so a client that only typed a URL still\n    67\t   needs one; a stable service name keeps `attach!` honest across endpoint\n    68\t   restarts.\"\n    69\t  \"yin.repl/repl\")\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\t(def requests-identity\n    73\t  \"The mirror table identity the server enters with surface #{:writer}: a\n    74\t   client's reflection of it writes eval requests.\"\n    75\t  \"yin.repl/requests\")\n    76\t\n    77\t\n    78\t(def answers-identity\n    79\t  \"The mirror table identity the server enters with surface #{:reader}: a\n    80\t   client's reflection of it reads answers.\"\n    81\t  \"yin.repl/answers\")\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\t(def ^:private diagnostic-bounds\n    85\t  \"Bound on operator-facing diagnostic text built from unbounded internal\n    86\t   state (raw connect URLs).\"\n    87\t  {:depth 3 :items 8 :chars 200})\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(def outcome-key :yin.repl.connect/outcome)\n    91\t(def connection-key :yin.repl.connect/connection)\n    92\t(def client-key :yin.repl.connect/client)\n    93\t(def descriptor-key :yin.repl.connect/descriptor)\n    94\t(def message-key :yin.repl.connect/message)\n    95\t(def event-key :yin.repl.connect/event)\n    96\t(def text-key :yin.repl.connect/text)\n    97\t\n    98\t\n    99\t;; =============================================================================\n   100\t;; Canonical request-target paths\n   101\t;; =============================================================================\n   102\t\n   103\t(def ^:private ascii-printable\n   104\t  \" !\\\"#$%&'()*+,-./0123456789:;<=>?@ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ[\\\\]^_`abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz{|}~\")\n   105\t\n   106\t\n   107\t(def ^:private unreserved\n   108\t  (set (map str (seq \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789-._~\"))))\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\t(def ^:private hex-values\n   112\t  (merge (zipmap (map str (seq \"0123456789\")) (range 10))\n   113\t         (zipmap (map str (seq \"abcdef\")) (range 10 16))\n   114\t         (zipmap (map str (seq \"ABCDEF\")) (range 10 16))))\n   115\t\n   116\t\n   117\t(def ^:private digits (set (map str (seq \"0123456789\"))))\n   118\t\n   119\t\n   120\t(defn- at\n   121\t  \"One character of `s` as a one-character string, so nothing here depends on a\n   122\t   host's character representation.\"\n   123\t  [s i]\n   124\t  (subs s i (inc i)))\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\t(defn- octet->char\n   128\t  [code]\n   129\t  (when (and (<= 32 code) (<= code 126))\n   130\t    (subs ascii-printable (- code 32) (- code 31))))\n   131\t\n   132\t\n   133\t(defn- percent-canonical\n   134\t  \"Decode percent-encoded unreserved octets and upper-case every remaining\n   135\t   percent hex pair.  An encoded slash is not unreserved, so it stays encoded.\"\n   136\t  [s]\n   137\t  (let [n (count s)]\n   138\t    (loop [i 0\n   139\t           out []]\n   140\t      (if (>= i n)\n   141\t        (str/join out)\n   142\t        (let [c (at s i)\n   143\t              hi (when (< (+ i 2) n) (get hex-values (at s (+ i 1))))\n   144\t              lo (when (< (+ i 2) n) (get hex-values (at s (+ i 2))))]\n   145\t          (if (and (= \"%\" c) hi lo)\n   146\t            (let [decoded (octet->char (+ (* 16 hi) lo))]\n   147\t              (if (contains? unreserved decoded)\n   148\t                (recur (+ i 3) (conj out decoded))\n   149\t                (recur (+ i 3) (conj out (str \"%\" (str/upper-case (subs s (inc i) (+ i 3))))))))\n   150\t            (recur (inc i) (conj out c))))))))\n   151\t\n   152\t\n   153\t(defn- drop-last-segment\n   154\t  [out]\n   155\t  (if-let [i (str/last-index-of out \"/\")]\n   156\t    (subs out 0 i)\n   157\t    \"\"))\n   158\t\n   159\t\n   160\t(defn- next-segment-end\n   161\t  [s]\n   162\t  (or (str/index-of s \"/\" 1) (count s)))\n   163\t\n   164\t\n   165\t(defn- remove-dot-segments\n   166\t  \"RFC 3986's remove_dot_segments, so repeated slashes and a trailing slash stay\n   167\t   significant while `.` and `..` do not reach the exact served-path lookup.\"\n   168\t  [path]\n   169\t  (loop [in path\n   170\t         out \"\"]\n   171\t    (cond\n   172\t      (= \"\" in) out\n   173\t      (str/starts-with? in \"../\") (recur (subs in 3) out)\n   174\t      (str/starts-with? in \"./\") (recur (subs in 2) out)\n   175\t      (str/starts-with? in \"/./\") (recur (str \"/\" (subs in 3)) out)\n   176\t      (= \"/.\" in) (recur \"/\" out)\n   177\t      (str/starts-with? in \"/../\") (recur (str \"/\" (subs in 4)) (drop-last-segment out))\n   178\t      (= \"/..\" in) (recur \"/\" (drop-last-segment out))\n   179\t      (= \".\" in) (recur \"\" out)\n   180\t      (= \"..\" in) (recur \"\" out)\n   181\t      :else (let [end (next-segment-end in)]\n   182\t              (recur (subs in end) (str out (subs in 0 end)))))))\n   183\t\n   184\t\n   185\t(defn- path-component\n   186\t  \"The URI path component of `raw`: everything before the first query or\n   187\t   fragment delimiter.\"\n   188\t  [raw]\n   189\t  (let [raw (str raw)\n   190\t        cut (->> [(str/index-of raw \"?\") (str/index-of raw \"#\")]\n   191\t                 (filter some?)\n   192\t                 (reduce min (count raw)))]\n   193\t    (subs raw 0 cut)))\n   194\t\n   195\t\n   196\t(defn canonical-path\n   197\t  \"The canonical, non-empty absolute request-target path of `raw`.\n   198\t\n   199\t   Query and fragment are ignored for lookup and absent from the descriptor,\n   200\t   dot segments are removed, percent-encoded unreserved octets are decoded, and\n   201\t   remaining percent hex digits are upper-case.  An empty URI path becomes `/`;\n   202\t   substituting the REPL's own default for an absent path is `repl-target`'s\n   203\t   job, and happens before this generic canonicalizer runs.\"\n   204\t  [raw]\n   205\t  (let [path (path-component raw)\n   206\t        path (if (str/starts-with? path \"/\") path (str \"/\" path))\n   207\t        path (percent-canonical (remove-dot-segments path))]\n   208\t    (if (= \"\" path) \"/\" path)))\n   209\t\n   210\t\n   211\t(defn repl-target\n   212\t  \"The REPL wrapper's rule: an empty raw URL path names `/repl`, and an explicit\n   213\t   `/` remains `/`.  Emptiness is a fact about the URI path component, so\n   214\t   `ws://host:port?x=1` carries no path and names `/repl` too.\"\n   215\t  [raw]\n   216\t  (if (= \"\" (path-component raw))\n   217\t    repl-path\n   218\t    (canonical-path raw)))\n   219\t\n   220\t\n   221\t;; =============================================================================\n   222\t;; URL to descriptor\n   223\t;; =============================================================================\n   224\t\n   225\t(defn- failure\n   226\t  [outcome message]\n   227\t  {outcome-key outcome message-key message})\n   228\t\n   229\t\n   230\t(defn- parse-port\n   231\t  [text]\n   232\t  (when (and (seq text) (every? #(contains? digits %) (map str (seq text))))\n   233\t    (loop [i 0 acc 0]\n   234\t      (if (>= i (count text))\n   235\t        (when (pos? acc) acc)\n   236\t        (recur (inc i) (+ (* 10 acc) (get hex-values (at text i))))))))\n   237\t\n   238\t\n   239\t(defn- authority-end\n   240\t  [s]\n   241\t  (->> [(str/index-of s \"/\") (str/index-of s \"?\") (str/index-of s \"#\")]\n   242\t       (filter some?)\n   243\t       (reduce min (count s))))\n   244\t\n   245\t\n   246\t(defn parse-url\n   247\t  \"Parse one REPL connect URL into a WebSocket descriptor.\n   248\t\n   249\t   Accepted forms are `daostream:ws://host[:port][/path]` and the same URL\n   250\t   without the `daostream:` prefix.  Bracketed IPv6 literals are out of this\n   251\t   slice and are reported rather than silently mis-parsed.\"\n   252\t  ([url] (parse-url url {}))\n   253\t  ([url {:keys [identity]}]\n   254\t   (let [url (str/trim (str url))\n   255\t         body (if (str/starts-with? url url-prefix) (subs url (count url-prefix)) url)]\n   256\t     (cond\n   257\t       (str/starts-with? body secure-scheme)\n   258\t       (failure :yin.repl.connect/invalid-url\n   259\t                \"wss:// has no settled descriptor form in this slice; use ws://\")\n   260\t\n   261\t       (not (str/starts-with? body ws-scheme))\n   262\t       (failure :yin.repl.connect/invalid-url\n   263\t                (str \"connect needs a daostream:ws:// URL; got \"\n   264\t                     (pr-str (data/summarize url diagnostic-bounds))))\n   265\t\n   266\t       :else\n   267\t       (let [rest-url (subs body (count ws-scheme))\n   268\t             end (authority-end rest-url)\n   269\t             authority (subs rest-url 0 end)\n   270\t             raw-path (subs rest-url end)\n   271\t             colon (str/last-index-of authority \":\")\n   272\t             host (if colon (subs authority 0 colon) authority)\n   273\t             port (if colon (parse-port (subs authority (inc colon))) default-port)]\n   274\t         (cond\n   275\t           (str/starts-with? authority \"[\")\n   276\t           (failure :yin.repl.connect/invalid-url\n   277\t                    \"bracketed IPv6 authorities are not part of this slice\")\n   278\t\n   279\t           (str/blank? host)\n   280\t           (failure :yin.repl.connect/invalid-url\n   281\t                    (str \"connect URL has no host: \"\n   282\t                         (pr-str (data/summarize url diagnostic-bounds))))\n   283\t\n   284\t           (nil? port)\n   285\t           (failure :yin.repl.connect/invalid-url\n   286\t                    (str \"connect URL port must be a positive integer: \"\n   287\t                         (pr-str (data/summarize url diagnostic-bounds))))\n   288\t\n   289\t           :else\n   290\t           (let [descriptor {:dao.stream/type ws/transport-type\n   291\t                             :dao.stream/identity (or identity service-identity)\n   292\t                             :ws/host host\n   293\t                             :ws/port port\n   294\t                             :ws/path (repl-target raw-path)}]\n   295\t             (if (ws/descriptor? descriptor)\n   296\t               {outcome-key :yin.repl.connect/parsed descriptor-key descriptor}\n   297\t               (failure :yin.repl.connect/invalid-url\n   298\t                        (str \"connect URL does not name a servable stream: \"\n   299\t                             (pr-str (data/summarize url diagnostic-bounds))))))))))))\n   300\t\n   301\t\n   302\t;; =============================================================================\n   303\t;; The two-reflection boundary\n   304\t;; =============================================================================\n   305\t\n   306\t(defn- mint\n   307\t  [handle anchor]\n   308\t  (let [result (stream/cursor handle anchor)]\n   309\t    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n   310\t      (:dao.stream/cursor result))))\n   311\t\n   312\t\n   313\t(defn- remote-descriptor\n   314\t  [channel identity]\n   315\t  {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote\n   316\t   :dao.stream/identity identity\n   317\t   :dao.stream/channel channel})\n   318\t\n   319\t\n   320\t(defn- attacher\n   321\t  [traffic connect!]\n   322\t  (ws/make-attacher {:traffic {:dao.stream/handle traffic\n   323\t                               :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n   324\t                     :admission traffic-admission\n   325\t                     :connect! connect!}))\n   326\t\n   327\t\n   328\t(defn- attach-outcome-message\n   329\t  [url result]\n   330\t  (case (:dao.stream/outcome result)\n   331\t    :dao.stream/invalid-descriptor\n   332\t    (str \"The boundary refused the descriptor for \" url)\n   333\t\n   334\t    :dao.stream/transport-error\n   335\t    (str \"Could not start connecting to \" url\n   336\t         \"; this is a local reachability failure and may succeed on retry\")\n   337\t\n   338\t    (str \"Attaching to \" url \" answered \" (pr-str (:dao.stream/outcome result)))))\n   339\t\n   340\t\n   341\t(defn- fresh-dial\n   342\t  \"Compose one dial over a fresh traffic medium, its own fresh `attach!`\n   343\t   bound to that medium, and a fresh channel ring, before any attach.  A\n   344\t   reattachment composes a fresh dial with a fresh cursor, per\n   345\t   `dao.stream.ws-project/dial`'s own contract, and `attach!` is scoped to\n   346\t   the traffic medium it deposits into, so it must be rebuilt alongside\n   347\t   it -- reusing an old `attach!` over a new traffic medium would deposit\n   348\t   into the wrong buffer.\"\n   349\t  [host]\n   350\t  (let [traffic (:dao.stream/handle\n   351\t                  (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n   352\t                                 ring/capacity-key traffic-capacity}))\n   353\t        attach! (try (attacher traffic (:connect! host))\n   354\t                     (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil))\n   355\t        cursor (mint traffic stream/anchor-newest)\n   356\t        ring (:dao.stream/handle\n   357\t               (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n   358\t                              ring/capacity-key traffic-capacity}))]\n   359\t    (when (and (some? attach!) (some? cursor))\n   360\t      (ws-project/dial {:attach! attach!\n   361\t                        :traffic {:dao.stream/handle traffic}\n   362\t                        :cursor cursor\n   363\t                        :ring ring\n   364\t                        :table {}}))))\n   365\t\n   366\t\n   367\t(defn- attach-pair\n   368\t  \"Attach both `requests`/`answers` reflections through `dial`'s one link,\n   369\t   sharing it exactly as `dao.stream.remote.cljc`'s attacher requires.\n   370\t   Returns `[requests-result answers-result]`, the second nil once the\n   371\t   first fails.\"\n   372\t  [dial channel]\n   373\t  (let [requests-result\n   374\t        (ws-project/dial-attach! dial (remote-descriptor channel\n   375\t                                                          requests-identity))]\n   376\t    (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome requests-result))\n   377\t      [requests-result nil]\n   378\t      [requests-result\n   379\t       (ws-project/dial-reflect! dial (remote-descriptor channel\n   380\t                                                          answers-identity))])))\n   381\t\n   382\t\n   383\t(defn open\n   384\t  \"Dial one WebSocket channel and attach both reflections, returning\n   385\t   immediately.  `attach!` over `dao.stream.remote` answers ok at once --\n   386\t   the contract's deferred remote confirmation -- so a successful result\n   387\t   is reported `:established` without waiting on any further transport\n   388\t   event.  The RPC client's response cursor is the `:dao.stream/newest`\n   389\t   anchor; `rpc/poll!` resolves it, retrying while the answers reflection\n   390\t   answers a retryable mint.\"\n   391\t  [{:keys [url identity host]}]\n   392\t  (let [parsed (parse-url url {:identity identity})]\n   393\t    (if-not (= :yin.repl.connect/parsed (get parsed outcome-key))\n   394\t      parsed\n   395\t      (let [channel (get parsed descriptor-key)]\n   396\t        (if-not (host-common/adapter? host)\n   397\t          (failure :yin.repl.connect/no-host-adapter\n   398\t                   (host-common/missing-message \"(connect …) is not wired\"))\n   399\t          (let [dial (fresh-dial host)]\n   400\t            (if-not dial\n   401\t              (failure :yin.repl.connect/invalid-composition\n   402\t                       \"The client boundary composition was refused\")\n   403\t              (let [[requests-result answers-result]\n   404\t                    (attach-pair dial channel)]\n   405\t                (cond\n   406\t                  (not= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome requests-result))\n   407\t                  (failure :yin.repl.connect/attach-failed\n   408\t                           (attach-outcome-message url requests-result))\n   409\t\n   410\t                  (not= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answers-result))\n   411\t                  (failure :yin.repl.connect/attach-failed\n   412\t                           (attach-outcome-message url answers-result))\n   413\t\n   414\t                  :else\n   415\t                  {outcome-key :yin.repl.connect/attached\n   416\t                   connection-key {:url url\n   417\t                                   :channel channel\n   418\t                                   :host host\n   419\t                                   :dial dial\n   420\t                                   :status :established\n   421\t                                   :detached-by nil}\n   422\t                   client-key (rpc/client-state\n   423\t                                (:dao.stream/handle requests-result)\n   424\t                                (:dao.stream/handle answers-result)\n   425\t                                stream/anchor-newest)})))))))))\n   426\t\n   427\t\n   428\t(defn step!\n   429\t  \"Drive this connection's dial one tick: its projection, so wire bytes the\n   430\t   host deposited onto the traffic medium reach the reflections' local\n   431\t   channel ring, then this end's own mirror step (a REPL client serves\n   432\t   nothing through it, but the composition is symmetric).  A caller's own\n   433\t   cadence must call this every tick it also polls the RPC client, or the\n   434\t   channel ring never receives anything the server sent -- reading a\n   435\t   reflection drains only the ring, never the traffic medium directly.\"\n   436\t  [connection]\n   437\t  (when-let [dial (:dial connection)]\n   438\t    (ws-project/dial-step! dial))\n   439\t  connection)\n   440\t\n   441\t\n   442\t(def terminal-statuses\n   443\t  \"Statuses observed from the RPC client's own `:terminal`.  They are\n   444\t   conclusions, so a later local action cannot overwrite them with an\n   445\t   intention.\"\n   446\t  #{:detached :ended :not-found :transport-error})\n   447\t\n   448\t\n   449\t(defn close!\n   450\t  \"Disconnect.  `close!` on the dialed channel's handle ends the connection;\n   451\t   the RPC client observes the loss on its next poll as `/detached`, which\n   452\t   is what keeps the connection reattachable.\n   453\t\n   454\t   Who asked is recorded, because the two detachments mean different things to\n   455\t   the shell: an operator `(disconnect)` returns ordinary input to local\n   456\t   evaluation, while an uninvited drop queues it until a reattachment decision\n   457\t   is made.  The terminal fact alone cannot tell them apart.\n   458\t\n   459\t   A status already observed is kept: `:closing` describes an intention, and\n   460\t   replacing an observed ending with it would lose the only record of how the\n   461\t   connection actually ended.\"\n   462\t  ([connection] (close! connection :operator))\n   463\t  ([connection by]\n   464\t   (when-let [ch (some-> (:dial connection) ws-project/channel)]\n   465\t     (stream/close! (:handle ch)))\n   466\t   (cond-> (assoc connection :detached-by by)\n   467\t     (not (contains? terminal-statuses (:status connection)))\n   468\t     (assoc :status :closing))))\n   469\t\n   470\t\n   471\t(defn operator-detached?\n   472\t  \"True while this connection is detached, or detaching, at the operator's own\n   473\t   request.\"\n   474\t  [connection]\n   475\t  (= :operator (:detached-by connection)))\n   476\t\n   477\t\n   478\t(defn reattachable?\n   479\t  \"True when the RPC client's terminal reason is the one reconnectable one.\"\n   480\t  [client]\n   481\t  (= :dao.stream.apply/detached (:terminal client)))\n   482\t\n   483\t\n   484\t(defn reattach\n   485\t  \"Reattach an existing connection: a fresh dial through the same host\n   486\t   adapter, both reflections attached again, then `rpc/rebind`.\n   487\t\n   488\t   The RPC client's response cursor and its collision-checked random id\n   489\t   allocator survive; only the writer and reader reflections change.\"\n   490\t  [connection client]\n   491\t  (if-not (reattachable? client)\n   492\t    (failure :yin.repl.connect/not-reattachable\n   493\t             (str \"Only a dropped connection reattaches; this one ended as \"\n   494\t                  (pr-str (:terminal client))))\n   495\t    (let [{:keys [url channel host]} connection\n   496\t          dial (fresh-dial host)]\n   497\t      (if-not dial\n   498\t        (failure :yin.repl.connect/invalid-composition\n   499\t                 \"The traffic medium minted no cursor\")\n   500\t        (let [[requests-result answers-result] (attach-pair dial channel)]\n   501\t          (cond\n   502\t            (not= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome requests-result))\n   503\t            (failure :yin.repl.connect/attach-failed\n   504\t                     (attach-outcome-message url requests-result))\n   505\t\n   506\t            (not= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answers-result))\n   507\t            (failure :yin.repl.connect/attach-failed\n   508\t                     (attach-outcome-message url answers-result))\n   509\t\n   510\t            :else\n   511\t            {outcome-key :yin.repl.connect/reattached\n   512\t             connection-key (assoc connection\n   513\t                                   :dial dial\n   514\t                                   :status :established\n   515\t                                   :detached-by nil)\n   516\t             client-key (rpc/rebind client\n   517\t                                    (:dao.stream/handle requests-result)\n   518\t                                    (:dao.stream/handle answers-result))}))))))\n   519\t\n   520\t\n   521\t;; =============================================================================\n   522\t;; Terminal status, observed from the RPC client\n   523\t;; =============================================================================\n   524\t\n   525\t(defn- event\n   526\t  [kind text]\n   527\t  {event-key kind text-key text})\n   528\t\n   529\t\n   530\t(defn- terminal-transition\n   531\t  [connection terminal]\n   532\t  (case terminal\n   533\t    :dao.stream.apply/detached\n   534\t    [:detached (event :yin.repl.connect/detached\n   535\t                      (str \"Disconnected from \" (:url connection)\n   536\t                           \"; the served stream is untouched, so (connect \"\n   537\t                           (pr-str (:url connection)) \") reattaches\"))]\n   538\t\n   539\t    :dao.stream.apply/ended\n   540\t    [:ended (event :yin.repl.connect/ended\n   541\t                   (str \"The stream served at \" (:url connection)\n   542\t                        \" ended; there is nothing to reattach to\"))]\n   543\t\n   544\t    :dao.stream.apply/not-found\n   545\t    [:not-found (event :yin.repl.connect/not-found\n   546\t                       (str \"No stream is served at \"\n   547\t                            (:ws/path (:channel connection))\n   548\t                            \": the endpoint disclaimed it, so this is not \"\n   549\t                            \"retried\"))]\n   550\t\n   551\t    :dao.stream.apply/transport-error\n   552\t    [:transport-error\n   553\t     (event :yin.repl.connect/transport-error\n   554\t           (str \"Could not reach \" (:url connection)\n   555\t                \"; this is a reachability failure and may succeed on retry\"))]\n   556\t\n   557\t    nil))\n   558\t\n   559\t\n   560\t(defn observe-terminal\n   561\t  \"Given `connection` and the RPC client's current `:terminal`, return\n   562\t   `[connection event]`.  The first terminal fact is the binding's\n   563\t   conclusion, published once: a connection already at a terminal status is\n   564\t   left alone, since a close/error race may repeat the same terminal on a\n   565\t   later poll.\"\n   566\t  [connection terminal]\n   567\t  (if (or (nil? terminal) (contains? terminal-statuses (:status connection)))\n   568\t    [connection nil]\n   569\t    (if-let [[status ev] (terminal-transition connection terminal)]\n   570\t      [(assoc connection :status status) ev]\n   571\t      [connection nil])))\n   572\t\n   573\t\n   574\t(defn summary\n   575\t  \"A serializable summary for `(repl-state)`.\"\n   576\t  [connection]\n   577\t  (if-not connection\n   578\t    {:connected? false}\n   579\t    {:connected? (= :established (:status connection))\n   580\t     :url (:url connection)\n   581\t     :path (:ws/path (:channel connection))\n   582\t     :identity (:dao.stream/identity (:channel connection))\n   583\t     :status (:status connection)\n   584\t     :attachment (:attachment (some-> (:dial connection) ws-project/channel))}))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The main composition now uses a shared request and answer pair. I’m checking two boundary cases before signing off: how an unresolved answer cursor reports remote failure, and whether the WebSocket retirement removed the old served-path behavior completely."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc | sed -n '400,570p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc | sed -n '130,410p'; nl -ba test/dao/stream/ws/node_test.cljs | sed -n '1,330p'; nl -ba test/dao/lease_composition_test.cljc | sed -n '700,880p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc | sed -n '400,570p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc | sed -n '130,410p'; nl -ba test/dao/stream/ws/node_test.cljs | sed -n '1,330p'; nl -ba test/dao/lease_composition_test.cljc | sed -n '700,880p'\"","aggregated_output":"   400\t                    {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   401\t                     :dao.stream/handle handle\n   402\t                     :dao.stream/attachment id})\n   403\t                (outcome :dao.stream/transport-error)))\n   404\t            (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   405\t              (outcome :dao.stream/transport-error))))))))\n   406\t\n   407\t\n   408\t;; Server acceptance is intentionally an endpoint composition object, not a\n   409\t;; global transport directory.  Its slots are supplied and owned by the host.\n   410\t;; Deferred retirement (dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md, slice 3,\n   411\t;; round 2): the :served table and the accept/disclaim handshake go once the\n   412\t;; mirror answers not-found per identity; they stay until dao.stream.serving,\n   413\t;; which routes accepted offers by these descriptors, is deleted with its\n   414\t;; consumers in slices 4 and 5.\n   415\t(defn make-endpoint\n   416\t  [{:keys [served control control-admission slots codecs] :as config}]\n   417\t  (let [control-target (checked-target control control-admission)\n   418\t        codecs (or codecs [transit/profile])]\n   419\t    (when-not (and (map? served) (seq slots))\n   420\t      (throw (ex-info \"WebSocket endpoint needs served paths and handoff slots\" {:config config})))\n   421\t    (when-not (and (seq codecs) (every? codec-profile? codecs))\n   422\t      (throw (ex-info \"WebSocket endpoint needs at least one codec profile\" {:codecs codecs})))\n   423\t    (when-not (apply distinct? (map :ws/subprotocol codecs))\n   424\t      (throw (ex-info \"WebSocket endpoint codec subprotocols must be distinct\" {:codecs codecs})))\n   425\t    (when-not (= :portable-values (:value-domain control-admission))\n   426\t      (throw (ex-info \"endpoint control medium must carry portable values\" {:admission control-admission})))\n   427\t    (doseq [[path descriptor] served]\n   428\t      ;; A served descriptor crosses under every profile the endpoint speaks,\n   429\t      ;; or the profile that cannot carry it must not be offered.\n   430\t      (when-not (and (= path (:ws/path descriptor))\n   431\t                     (every? #(descriptor? descriptor %) codecs))\n   432\t        (throw (ex-info \"invalid served descriptor\" {:path path :descriptor descriptor}))))\n   433\t    (doseq [slot slots]\n   434\t      (checked-target (:offer slot) (:offer-admission slot))\n   435\t      (checked-target (:ack slot) (:ack-admission slot))\n   436\t      (when-not (and (= 1 (get-in slot [:offer-admission :capacity]))\n   437\t                     (= :host-values (get-in slot [:offer-admission :value-domain]))\n   438\t                     (= 1 (get-in slot [:ack-admission :capacity]))\n   439\t                     (= :host-values (get-in slot [:ack-admission :value-domain]))\n   440\t                     (some? (:ack-cursor slot)))\n   441\t        (throw (ex-info \"invalid capacity-one WebSocket handoff slot\" {:slot slot}))))\n   442\t    {:config config\n   443\t     :codecs codecs\n   444\t     :codec-index (zipmap (map :ws/subprotocol codecs) codecs)\n   445\t     :state (atom {:control control-target\n   446\t                   :slots (mapv (fn [slot]\n   447\t                                  (assoc slot :status :free)) slots)\n   448\t                   :connections {}})}))\n   449\t\n   450\t\n   451\t(defn endpoint-state\n   452\t  [endpoint]\n   453\t  @(:state endpoint))\n   454\t\n   455\t\n   456\t(defn- endpoint-target\n   457\t  [endpoint]\n   458\t  (:control (endpoint-state endpoint)))\n   459\t\n   460\t\n   461\t(defn- release-slot!\n   462\t  \"Return one handoff slot to the bounded free pool and forget the connection it\n   463\t   held.  Releasing drops the retained handle: a released slot's acknowledgement\n   464\t   is stale by construction, so nothing may resolve through it afterwards.\"\n   465\t  [endpoint index attachment]\n   466\t  (swap! (:state endpoint)\n   467\t         (fn [s]\n   468\t           (-> s\n   469\t               (update-in [:slots index] dissoc\n   470\t                          :attachment :handle :handle-state :codec :opened-at)\n   471\t               (assoc-in [:slots index :status] :free)\n   472\t               (update :connections dissoc attachment)))))\n   473\t\n   474\t\n   475\t(defn accept-connection!\n   476\t  \"Bounded upgrade callback entry.  A bad path or exhausted slots is closed\n   477\t   immediately; a valid path deposits precisely one host-local offer and waits\n   478\t   for `endpoint-step` to consume a matching acknowledgement.\n   479\t\n   480\t   The socket seam may carry `:ws/subprotocol`, the subprotocol the host\n   481\t   negotiated for this upgrade.  An endpoint serves every profile it was\n   482\t   composed with, concurrently and through the same served paths; a named\n   483\t   subprotocol it does not speak is a refused handshake, never a downgrade,\n   484\t   and an absent name is the Transit default for sockets that negotiated\n   485\t   nothing (direct composition and tests).\"\n   486\t  ([endpoint path socket] (accept-connection! endpoint path socket nil))\n   487\t  ([endpoint path socket now]\n   488\t   (let [{:keys [served]} (:config endpoint)\n   489\t         offered (:ws/subprotocol socket)\n   490\t         codec (if (nil? offered)\n   491\t                 transit/profile\n   492\t                 (get (:codec-index endpoint) offered))\n   493\t         descriptor (get served path)]\n   494\t     (cond\n   495\t       (nil? codec)\n   496\t       (do (invoke-close! socket protocol-close-code \"dao.stream/subprotocol-unsupported\")\n   497\t           {:ws/status :ws/unsupported-subprotocol})\n   498\t\n   499\t       (nil? descriptor)\n   500\t       (do (send-result socket ((:ws/encode codec) {:ws/frame :ws/disclaim}))\n   501\t           (invoke-close! socket disclaim-close-code \"dao.stream/not-found\")\n   502\t           {:ws/status :ws/disclaimed})\n   503\t\n   504\t       :else\n   505\t       (let [state (:state endpoint)\n   506\t             chosen (volatile! nil)]\n   507\t         ;; Claim before depositing.  The offer append may synchronously invoke\n   508\t         ;; host code, so leaving the slot `:free` until after it returns would\n   509\t         ;; permit a second upgrade callback to overwrite the sole offer.\n   510\t         (swap! state (fn [s]\n   511\t                        (if-let [[index slot] (first (keep-indexed (fn [i x]\n   512\t                                                                     (when (= :free (:status x)) [i x]))\n   513\t                                                                   (:slots s)))]\n   514\t                          (do (vreset! chosen [index slot])\n   515\t                              (assoc-in s [:slots index :status] :reserving))\n   516\t                          s)))\n   517\t         (if-not @chosen\n   518\t           (do (invoke-close! socket 1013 \"dao.stream/acceptance-full\")\n   519\t               {:ws/status :ws/full})\n   520\t           (let [[index slot] @chosen\n   521\t                 id (attachment-id)\n   522\t                 [handle hstate] (new-handle descriptor id (endpoint-target endpoint) :pending socket codec)\n   523\t                 offer {:ws/attachment id :ws/event :ws/accepted\n   524\t                        :ws/handle {:dao.stream/handle handle\n   525\t                                    :dao.stream/surface #{:writer :closable}}}\n   526\t                 result (stream/append! (:dao.stream/handle (:offer slot)) offer)]\n   527\t             (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n   528\t               (do (swap! state (fn [s]\n   529\t                                  (-> s\n   530\t                                      (assoc-in [:slots index :status] :pending)\n   531\t                                      (assoc-in [:slots index :attachment] id)\n   532\t                                      (assoc-in [:slots index :handle] handle)\n   533\t                                      (assoc-in [:slots index :handle-state] hstate)\n   534\t                                      (assoc-in [:slots index :codec] codec)\n   535\t                                      (assoc-in [:slots index :opened-at] now)\n   536\t                                      (assoc-in [:connections id] handle))))\n   537\t                   {:ws/status :ws/pending :ws/attachment id :ws/handle handle})\n   538\t               (do (swap! hstate assoc :phase :closed)\n   539\t                   (invoke-close! socket 1011 \"dao.stream/offer-failed\")\n   540\t                   (release-slot! endpoint index id)\n   541\t                   {:ws/status :ws/offer-failed})))))))))\n   542\t\n   543\t\n   544\t(defn- valid-ack?\n   545\t  [ack attachment]\n   546\t  (and (map? ack)\n   547\t       (= attachment (:ws/attachment ack))\n   548\t       (= :ws/accept (:ws/command ack))\n   549\t       (writer-target? (:ws/deposit ack))\n   550\t       (admission? (:ws/admission ack))))\n   551\t\n   552\t\n   553\t;; Deferred retirement: the wire {:ws/frame :ws/accept} answer to an\n   554\t;; acknowledgement goes with the served-path table and the disclaim frame\n   555\t;; (slices 4 and 5); the copy path's clients still resolve on receiving it.\n   556\t(defn- accept-slot!\n   557\t  [endpoint index slot ack]\n   558\t  (let [hstate (:handle-state slot)\n   559\t        socket (:socket @hstate)\n   560\t        codec (:codec slot)\n   561\t        target (:ws/deposit ack)]\n   562\t    (swap! hstate assoc :deposit target :phase :open :resolution? true)\n   563\t    (let [sent (send-result socket ((:ws/encode codec) {:ws/frame :ws/accept}))]\n   564\t      (when-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome sent))\n   565\t        (swap! hstate assoc :phase :closed)\n   566\t        (invoke-close! socket 1011 \"dao.stream/accept-failed\")\n   567\t        (terminal! hstate (:attachment slot) :ws/closed))\n   568\t      ;; Either way the endpoint is done with this connection: the composition\n   569\t      ;; owns an accepted session, and a failed acceptance is already torn down.\n   570\t      (release-slot! endpoint index (:attachment slot)))))\n   130\t  \"True once the projection stopped: the ring was closed by a terminal\n   131\t   lifecycle event or a failure resolution, or the traffic medium\n   132\t   itself answered end.\"\n   133\t  [project]\n   134\t  (:closed? @project))\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\t(defn reading-cursor\n   138\t  \"The projection's current reading cursor on the traffic medium.\"\n   139\t  [project]\n   140\t  (:cursor @project))\n   141\t\n   142\t\n   143\t;; =============================================================================\n   144\t;; The accepting peer (section 5: accept, project, mirror)\n   145\t;; =============================================================================\n   146\t\n   147\t(defn- writer-target?\n   148\t  [x]\n   149\t  (and (map? x)\n   150\t       (stream/writer? (:dao.stream/handle x))\n   151\t       (contains? (:dao.stream/surface x) :writer)))\n   152\t\n   153\t\n   154\t(defn- valid-slot?\n   155\t  [{:keys [offer-reader offer-cursor ack-writer]}]\n   156\t  (and (stream/reader? offer-reader)\n   157\t       (some? offer-cursor)\n   158\t       (writer-target? ack-writer)))\n   159\t\n   160\t\n   161\t(defn make-acceptor\n   162\t  \"Compose the accepting end of the spec's section-5 toy.\n   163\t   `:endpoint` is a dao.stream.ws/make-endpoint value whose handoff\n   164\t   `:slots` are given here, in endpoint order, as {:offer-reader r\n   165\t   :offer-cursor c :ack-writer target} -- readers, cursors and writers\n   166\t   the composition minted before the listener started. `:table` is the\n   167\t   mirror's table (dao.stream.remote.md 2.2). `:make-media` receives\n   168\t   one accepted offer and returns the attachment's composition:\n   169\t   :traffic (the deposit target the acknowledgement carries),\n   170\t   :admission (its declaration), :reader (the traffic reader the\n   171\t   projection reads), :cursor (its minted reading cursor) and :ring\n   172\t   (the fresh channel ring buffer). The listener is the host's: it\n   173\t   calls ws/accept-connection! on this endpoint, per dao.stream.ws.md\n   174\t   Serving.\"\n   175\t  [{:keys [endpoint slots table make-media] :as config}]\n   176\t  (when-not (and (map? config)\n   177\t                 (some? endpoint)\n   178\t                 (fn? make-media)\n   179\t                 (map? table)\n   180\t                 (seq slots)\n   181\t                 (every? valid-slot? slots))\n   182\t    (throw (ex-info \"invalid DaoStream ws acceptor composition\"\n   183\t                    {:config config})))\n   184\t  (atom {:endpoint endpoint\n   185\t         :slots (vec slots)\n   186\t         :table table\n   187\t         :make-media make-media\n   188\t         :offer-cursors (mapv :offer-cursor slots)\n   189\t         :sessions {}}))\n   190\t\n   191\t\n   192\t(defn- adopt!\n   193\t  \"Adopt one accepted offer as a session: create the attachment's\n   194\t   media through :make-media, acknowledge the offer per\n   195\t   dao.stream.ws.md Serving (:ws/command :ws/accept, the deposit\n   196\t   target and its admission), and register the projection, ring,\n   197\t   reading cursor and socket handle the mirror works through. An\n   198\t   offer that is not an acceptance, and an acknowledgement the slot's\n   199\t   medium refuses, close the offered handle; the slot itself is the\n   200\t   endpoint's to release.\"\n   201\t  [acceptor slot offer]\n   202\t  (let [make-media (:make-media @acceptor)\n   203\t        handle (get-in offer [:ws/handle :dao.stream/handle])\n   204\t        attachment (:ws/attachment offer)]\n   205\t    (if-not (and (= :ws/accepted (:ws/event offer))\n   206\t                 (string? attachment)\n   207\t                 (some? handle)\n   208\t                 (stream/writer? handle)\n   209\t                 (stream/closable? handle))\n   210\t      (when (stream/closable? handle)\n   211\t        (stream/close! handle))\n   212\t      (let [media (make-media offer)\n   213\t            appended (stream/append!\n   214\t                       (:dao.stream/handle (:ack-writer slot))\n   215\t                       {:ws/attachment attachment\n   216\t                        :ws/command :ws/accept\n   217\t                        :ws/deposit (:traffic media)\n   218\t                        :ws/admission (:admission media)})]\n   219\t        (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome appended))\n   220\t          (swap! acceptor assoc-in [:sessions attachment]\n   221\t                 {:attachment attachment\n   222\t                  :handle handle\n   223\t                  :ring (:ring media)\n   224\t                  :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n   225\t                            (stream/cursor (:ring media)\n   226\t                                           stream/anchor-oldest))\n   227\t                  :project (projection\n   228\t                             {:attachment attachment\n   229\t                              :traffic (:reader media)\n   230\t                              :cursor (:cursor media)\n   231\t                              :ring (:ring media)})})\n   232\t          (stream/close! handle))))))\n   233\t\n   234\t\n   235\t(defn- reaped\n   236\t  \"The sessions without the closed ones. A closed session's tick just\n   237\t   ran its last mirror pass -- a closed ring forwards no further\n   238\t   request, so only what it retained could ever be answered, and that\n   239\t   pass answered what the handle accepted -- so its handle, ring and\n   240\t   projection have nothing left to do. Keeping them would grow the\n   241\t   composition without bound across repeated connections; the endpoint\n   242\t   released the connection's slot at acceptance (dao.stream.ws.md\n   243\t   Serving), and this is the composition's own bound.\"\n   244\t  [m]\n   245\t  (into {} (remove (fn [[_ s]] (closed? (:project s))) m)))\n   246\t\n   247\t\n   248\t(defn accept-step!\n   249\t  \"Advance the accepting composition one tick at `now`, in the order\n   250\t   serving compositions use: a transport step first (releasing dead\n   251\t   pendings, consuming standing acknowledgements), then one offer per\n   252\t   slot adopted with its fresh media and acknowledgement, then a\n   253\t   second transport step, so the fresh acknowledgement is consumed and\n   254\t   the accept frame is on the wire before this end answers anything,\n   255\t   then per session the projection and, over the projected reader and\n   256\t   the socket handle, the mirror step. A session whose projection has\n   257\t   closed is then removed: the mirror pass just run was its last, and\n   258\t   repeated connections must not accumulate. Returns the acceptor.\"\n   259\t  [acceptor now]\n   260\t  (let [{:keys [endpoint slots] :as s} @acceptor]\n   261\t    (ws/endpoint-step endpoint now)\n   262\t    (doseq [[index slot] (map-indexed vector slots)]\n   263\t      (let [r (stream/next (:offer-reader slot)\n   264\t                           (nth (:offer-cursors s) index))]\n   265\t        (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   266\t          (swap! acceptor assoc-in [:offer-cursors index]\n   267\t                 (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   268\t          (adopt! acceptor slot (:dao.stream/value r)))))\n   269\t    (ws/endpoint-step endpoint now)\n   270\t    (doseq [[attachment session] (:sessions @acceptor)]\n   271\t      (step! (:project session))\n   272\t      (swap! acceptor assoc-in [:sessions attachment :cursor]\n   273\t             (remote/mirror-step (:table @acceptor)\n   274\t                                 (:ring session)\n   275\t                                 (:cursor session)\n   276\t                                 (:handle session))))\n   277\t    (swap! acceptor update :sessions reaped)\n   278\t    acceptor))\n   279\t\n   280\t\n   281\t(defn sessions\n   282\t  \"The acceptor's sessions as data: attachment id -> {:attachment\n   283\t   :handle :ring :cursor :project}.\"\n   284\t  [acceptor]\n   285\t  (:sessions @acceptor))\n   286\t\n   287\t\n   288\t(defn session-end\n   289\t  \"One accepted attachment's channel end {:reader r :writer w} -- the\n   290\t   ring this end projects onto and the socket handle it writes\n   291\t   through: the entry for dao.stream.remote/attacher's\n   292\t   :dao.stream.remote/channels map at this end, so the accepting peer\n   293\t   can attach reflections of the other direction over the same\n   294\t   connection. Nil before the attachment is adopted and again once\n   295\t   its closed session is reaped.\"\n   296\t  [acceptor attachment]\n   297\t  (when-some [session (get (:sessions @acceptor) attachment)]\n   298\t    {:reader (:ring session) :writer (:handle session)}))\n   299\t\n   300\t\n   301\t;; =============================================================================\n   302\t;; The dialing peer (section 5: the link over its dialed attachment)\n   303\t;; =============================================================================\n   304\t\n   305\t(defn dial\n   306\t  \"Compose the dialing end of one WebSocket channel (3.1). `:attach!`\n   307\t   is the dao.stream.ws/make-attacher product whose :traffic deposit\n   308\t   medium is the same medium named by `:traffic` (its target), with\n   309\t   `:cursor` already minted on it before any attach!; `:ring` is the\n   310\t   channel ring buffer this end projects onto. `:table` names the\n   311\t   identities this peer serves over the dialed channel, so\n   312\t   `dial-step!` runs the projection and then this end's own mirror\n   313\t   step: the dialing end serves the other direction on the same\n   314\t   connection. `dial-attach!` takes a remote descriptor whose\n   315\t   :dao.stream/channel is this channel's ws descriptor: it attaches,\n   316\t   projects the attachment onto the ring, and answers through\n   317\t   dao.stream.remote/attacher with the channel end {:reader ring\n   318\t   :writer handle} -- the link's drain then runs inside every\n   319\t   reflection operation. One dial value carries one active\n   320\t   attachment; a reattachment composes a fresh dial with a fresh\n   321\t   cursor, as dao.stream.ws.md composes one medium per active client\n   322\t   attachment. :dao.stream.remote/events, :dao.stream.remote/resend-\n   323\t   after and :dao.stream.remote/budget pass to the attacher as its\n   324\t   policy.\"\n   325\t  [{:keys [attach! traffic cursor ring table] :as opts}]\n   326\t  (when-not (and (fn? attach!)\n   327\t                 (map? traffic)\n   328\t                 (stream/writer? (:dao.stream/handle traffic))\n   329\t                 (stream/reader? (:dao.stream/handle traffic))\n   330\t                 (some? cursor)\n   331\t                 (stream/reader? ring)\n   332\t                 (stream/writer? ring)\n   333\t                 (stream/closable? ring)\n   334\t                 (map? table))\n   335\t    (throw (ex-info \"invalid DaoStream ws dial composition\"\n   336\t                    {:opts opts})))\n   337\t  (let [channel (atom nil)\n   338\t        mirror-cursor (atom (:dao.stream/cursor\n   339\t                              (stream/cursor ring stream/anchor-oldest)))\n   340\t        policy (select-keys opts [:dao.stream.remote/events\n   341\t                                  :dao.stream.remote/resend-after\n   342\t                                  :dao.stream.remote/budget])]\n   343\t    (atom {:attach! attach! :traffic traffic :cursor cursor :ring ring\n   344\t           :table table :channel channel :mirror-cursor mirror-cursor\n   345\t           :policy policy})))\n   346\t\n   347\t\n   348\t(defn dial-attach!\n   349\t  \"Attach one reflection of `descriptor` (a :dao.stream/remote\n   350\t   descriptor) through the dialed channel: the ws attach runs first,\n   351\t   the attachment's projection is composed, and the remote attacher\n   352\t   answers with the reflection -- its confirmation deferred, per\n   353\t   dao.stream.remote.md 2.4, to the descriptor probe the link sends\n   354\t   now. A channel attach that fails answers the ws attacher's own\n   355\t   outcome. One dial value carries one active attachment: a dial that\n   356\t   has already attached rejects a further dial-attach! -- its ring\n   357\t   and traffic cursor already belong to the first attachment, and a\n   358\t   second projection on them would mix two attachments' state -- with\n   359\t   a composition error; a reattachment composes a fresh dial with a\n   360\t   fresh cursor, as `dial` documents. Returns the remote attach!\n   361\t   result.\"\n   362\t  [dial descriptor]\n   363\t  (let [{:keys [attach! traffic cursor ring channel policy]} @dial]\n   364\t    (when-some [attached @channel]\n   365\t      (throw (ex-info\n   366\t               \"this dial already attached its one active attachment\"\n   367\t               {:attachment (:attachment attached)\n   368\t                :reattachment \"compose a fresh dial with a fresh cursor\"})))\n   369\t    (let [r (attach! (:dao.stream/channel descriptor))]\n   370\t      (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   371\t        r\n   372\t        (let [cd (:dao.stream/channel descriptor)\n   373\t              handle (:dao.stream/handle r)\n   374\t              project (projection {:attachment (:dao.stream/attachment r)\n   375\t                                   :traffic (:dao.stream/handle traffic)\n   376\t                                   :cursor cursor\n   377\t                                   :ring ring})\n   378\t              reflect! (remote/attacher\n   379\t                         (merge policy\n   380\t                                {:dao.stream.remote/channels\n   381\t                                 {cd {:reader ring :writer handle}}}))]\n   382\t          (reset! channel {:attachment (:dao.stream/attachment r)\n   383\t                           :handle handle :project project\n   384\t                           :reflect! reflect!})\n   385\t          (reflect! descriptor))))))\n   386\t\n   387\t\n   388\t(defn dial-reflect!\n   389\t  \"Attach a further reflection of `descriptor` through a dial's already\n   390\t   established channel, sharing the one link `dial-attach!` created for\n   391\t   it: dao.stream.remote.cljc keeps one link per channel descriptor,\n   392\t   shared by every reflection through that channel, and `attacher`'s\n   393\t   returned function is exactly that per-channel sharing boundary.  A\n   394\t   dial with no established channel yet answers `:dao.stream/invalid-\n   395\t   descriptor`, since there is no attacher to share.\"\n   396\t  [dial descriptor]\n   397\t  (let [{:keys [channel]} @dial]\n   398\t    (if-some [reflect! (:reflect! @channel)]\n   399\t      (reflect! descriptor)\n   400\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-descriptor})))\n   401\t\n   402\t\n   403\t(defn dial-step!\n   404\t  \"Drive the dialing composition one tick, at the composition's\n   405\t   cadence: the attachment's projection first, so what the wire\n   406\t   deposited reaches the ring, then this end's own mirror step over\n   407\t   the projected reader and the socket handle, answering the other\n   408\t   direction's requests against this end's table. Returns the\n   409\t   mirror's advanced reading cursor.\"\n   410\t  [dial]\n     1\t(ns dao.stream.ws.node-test\n     2\t  \"Node host-adapter tests for the DaoStream v2 WebSocket boundary.\n     3\t\n     4\t   Two layers, deliberately separate:\n     5\t\n     6\t   * deterministic tests drive a fake host socket through the real adapter\n     7\t     wiring, so event translation, framing, and teardown are proven with\n     8\t     injected socket primitives and no network; and\n     9\t   * end-to-end tests bind a real `ws` listener on an ephemeral loopback port\n    10\t     and run the full client and serving compositions across real sockets.\n    11\t\n    12\t   The `ws` npm package (package.json) is the prerequisite for the second\n    13\t   layer.  Every driver below is an explicit test-owned ticker; the adapter\n    14\t   itself owns no cadence, cursor, medium, or registry.\"\n    15\t  (:require [\"ws\" :as ws-package]\n    16\t            [cljs.test :refer [async deftest is]]\n    17\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n    18\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    19\t            [dao.stream.cbor :as cbor]\n    20\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n    21\t            [dao.stream.transit :as transit]\n    22\t            [dao.stream.ws :as ws]\n    23\t            [dao.stream.ws.node :as node]\n    24\t            [dao.stream.ws-project :as project]))\n    25\t\n    26\t\n    27\t;; =============================================================================\n    28\t;; Explicit test composition data\n    29\t;; =============================================================================\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\t(def admission\n    33\t  {:retention :evict-oldest :capacity 64 :value-domain :portable-values})\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\t(def handoff-admission\n    37\t  {:retention :evict-oldest :capacity 1 :value-domain :host-values})\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\t(defn- buffer\n    41\t  ([] (buffer 64))\n    42\t  ([capacity]\n    43\t   (:dao.stream/handle (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n    44\t                                      ring/capacity-key capacity}))))\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\t(defn- newest\n    48\t  [handle]\n    49\t  (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-newest)))\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t(defn- drain\n    53\t  \"Collect every retained value from the oldest position.\"\n    54\t  [handle]\n    55\t  (loop [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-oldest))\n    56\t         seen []]\n    57\t    (let [result (stream/next handle cursor)]\n    58\t      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n    59\t        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor result) (conj seen (:dao.stream/value result)))\n    60\t        seen))))\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\t(defn- event-kinds\n    64\t  [handle]\n    65\t  (mapv (juxt :ws/event :ws/reason) (drain handle)))\n    66\t\n    67\t\n    68\t(defn- payload-values\n    69\t  \"The :ws/value of every :ws/payload envelope, in deposit order.\"\n    70\t  [events]\n    71\t  (mapv :ws/value (filter #(= :ws/payload (:ws/event %)) events)))\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t(defn- descriptor\n    75\t  ([] (descriptor \"/yin/repl\"))\n    76\t  ([path]\n    77\t   {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ws\n    78\t    :dao.stream/identity \"node-adapter-service\"\n    79\t    :ws/host \"127.0.0.1\"\n    80\t    :ws/port 9182\n    81\t    :ws/path path}))\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\t;; =============================================================================\n    85\t;; A deterministic fake host socket (injected socket primitives)\n    86\t;; =============================================================================\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t(defn- fake-socket\n    90\t  \"A recording stand-in for one `ws` socket: additive `.on` registration plus\n    91\t   the `send`/`close` surface `node/raw-socket` wraps.  `fire` replays the\n    92\t   host events the real library would emit.\"\n    93\t  []\n    94\t  (let [handlers (atom {})\n    95\t        sent (atom [])\n    96\t        closes (atom [])\n    97\t        socket (js-obj \"on\" (fn [event f] (swap! handlers assoc event f))\n    98\t                       ;; The host library's send returns nil; the fake must\n    99\t                       ;; answer with the same shape the transport classifies.\n   100\t                       \"send\" (fn [data] (swap! sent conj data) nil)\n   101\t                       \"close\" (fn [code reason] (swap! closes conj [code reason])))]\n   102\t    {:socket socket\n   103\t     :handlers handlers\n   104\t     :sent sent\n   105\t     :closes closes\n   106\t     :fire (fn [event & args]\n   107\t             (let [f (get @handlers event)]\n   108\t               (assert (some? f) (str \"no listener for host event \" event))\n   109\t               (apply f args)))}))\n   110\t\n   111\t\n   112\t(defn- fake-connect!\n   113\t  \"A `:connect!` seam whose host socket is the fake: the deterministic\n   114\t   loopback composition used where a real socket adds nothing.\"\n   115\t  [fake]\n   116\t  (fn [_descriptor adapter]\n   117\t    (node/wire! (:socket fake) adapter)\n   118\t    (node/raw-socket (:socket fake))))\n   119\t\n   120\t\n   121\t(defn- attach-with-fake\n   122\t  [traffic fake]\n   123\t  ((ws/make-attacher {:traffic {:dao.stream/handle traffic\n   124\t                                :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n   125\t                      :admission admission\n   126\t                      :connect! (fake-connect! fake)})\n   127\t   (descriptor)))\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t(defn- fire-text!\n   131\t  [fake value]\n   132\t  ((:fire fake) \"message\" (.from js/Buffer (transit/encode value)) false))\n   133\t\n   134\t\n   135\t;; =============================================================================\n   136\t;; Pure host-edge data\n   137\t;; =============================================================================\n   138\t\n   139\t\n   140\t(deftest canonical-path-follows-the-wire-spec\n   141\t  (is (= \"/yin/repl\" (node/canonical-path \"/yin/repl\")))\n   142\t  ;; Query and fragment are ignored for lookup and never reach the table.\n   143\t  (is (= \"/yin/repl\" (node/canonical-path \"/yin/repl?after=1\")))\n   144\t  (is (= \"/yin/repl\" (node/canonical-path \"/yin/repl#frag\")))\n   145\t  (is (= \"/yin/repl\" (node/canonical-path \"/yin/repl?a=b#frag\")))\n   146\t  ;; An empty path is the root; relative paths and dot segments normalize.\n   147\t  (is (= \"/\" (node/canonical-path \"\")))\n   148\t  (is (= \"/a/b\" (node/canonical-path \"/a/./b\")))\n   149\t  (is (= \"/b\" (node/canonical-path \"/a/../b\")))\n   150\t  (is (= \"/x\" (node/canonical-path \"/../../x\")))\n   151\t  ;; Repeated and trailing slashes are significant; encoded slashes are not.\n   152\t  (is (= \"/a//b\" (node/canonical-path \"/a//b\")))\n   153\t  (is (= \"/a/\" (node/canonical-path \"/a/\")))\n   154\t  ;; RFC 3986 keeps the trailing slash a final dot segment leaves behind, and\n   155\t  ;; the client canonicalizer (`yin.repl.connect`) agrees.\n   156\t  (is (= \"/a/\" (node/canonical-path \"/a/b/..\")))\n   157\t  (is (= \"/repl/\" (node/canonical-path \"/repl/.\")))\n   158\t  (is (= \"/\" (node/canonical-path \"/..\")))\n   159\t  (is (= \"/a%2Fb\" (node/canonical-path \"/a%2fb\")))\n   160\t  ;; Unreserved octets decode; remaining escapes upper-case.\n   161\t  (is (= \"/a~b\" (node/canonical-path \"/a%7Eb\")))\n   162\t  (is (= \"/A\" (node/canonical-path \"/%41\")))\n   163\t  (is (= \"/repl/%C3%A4\" (node/canonical-path \"/repl/%c3%a4\")))\n   164\t  (is (= \"/x\" (node/canonical-path \"/%2e%2e/x\")))\n   165\t  ;; Anything that cannot reach the canonical form is refused, not repaired.\n   166\t  (is (nil? (node/canonical-path \"yin/repl\")))\n   167\t  (is (nil? (node/canonical-path \"%zz\")))\n   168\t  (is (nil? (node/canonical-path \"/repl/%E\")))\n   169\t  (is (nil? (node/canonical-path \"/repl/%\")))\n   170\t  (is (nil? (node/canonical-path 42))))\n   171\t\n   172\t\n   173\t(deftest socket-url-uses-descriptor-reachability-only\n   174\t  (is (= \"ws://127.0.0.1:9182/yin/repl\"\n   175\t         (node/socket-url (descriptor))))\n   176\t  (is (= \"ws://example.org:9090/\"\n   177\t         (node/socket-url (assoc (descriptor \"/\") :ws/host \"example.org\" :ws/port 9090)))))\n   178\t\n   179\t\n   180\t;; =============================================================================\n   181\t;; Deterministic wiring through the fake socket\n   182\t;; =============================================================================\n   183\t\n   184\t\n   185\t(deftest wiring-translates-host-events-and-keeps-framing-honest\n   186\t  (let [traffic (buffer)\n   187\t        fake (fake-socket)\n   188\t        result (attach-with-fake traffic fake)\n   189\t        handle (:dao.stream/handle result)\n   190\t        me (:dao.stream/attachment result)]\n   191\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result)))\n   192\t    (is (string? me))\n   193\t    ;; The HTTP upgrade is never a resolution signal: only the three host\n   194\t    ;; events the boundary translates are subscribed, and 'open' is not among\n   195\t    ;; them.  The adapter is the socket's sole subscriber.\n   196\t    (is (= #{\"message\" \"close\" \"error\"} (set (keys @(:handlers fake)))))\n   197\t    ;; While establishing, append! answers full and nothing is sent.\n   198\t    (is (= :dao.stream/full (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! handle :early))))\n   199\t    (is (empty? @(:sent fake)))\n   200\t    ;; The first accept frame resolves the attachment; then append! frames.\n   201\t    (fire-text! fake {:ws/frame :ws/accept})\n   202\t    (is (= [[:ws/opened nil]] (event-kinds traffic)))\n   203\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! handle {:a 1}))))\n   204\t    (is (= [{:ws/frame :ws/value :ws/value {:a 1}}]\n   205\t           (mapv transit/decode @(:sent fake))))\n   206\t    ;; Inbound values are enveloped and attributed, never judged.\n   207\t    (fire-text! fake {:ws/frame :ws/value :ws/value [:yin :hi]})\n   208\t    (is (= [[:ws/opened nil] [:ws/payload nil]] (event-kinds traffic)))\n   209\t    (is (= [:yin :hi] (:ws/value (second (drain traffic)))))\n   210\t    (is (every? #(= me (:ws/attachment %)) (drain traffic)))\n   211\t    ;; A binary frame is undecodable by the text codec: the transport performs\n   212\t    ;; its own decode-failure teardown (deposit plus close 4002).\n   213\t    ((:fire fake) \"message\" (.from js/Buffer #js [0 1 2]) true)\n   214\t    (is (= [[:ws/opened nil] [:ws/payload nil] [:ws/error :ws/decode-failure]]\n   215\t           (event-kinds traffic)))\n   216\t    (is (= [ws/protocol-close-code \"dao.stream/protocol-error\"] (last @(:closes fake))))\n   217\t    ;; Host close completion deposits exactly one terminal event.\n   218\t    ((:fire fake) \"close\" ws/protocol-close-code \"dao.stream/protocol-error\")\n   219\t    (is (= [[:ws/opened nil] [:ws/payload nil] [:ws/error :ws/decode-failure]\n   220\t            [:ws/closed nil]]\n   221\t           (event-kinds traffic)))\n   222\t    (is (= :dao.stream/closed (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! handle :late))))\n   223\t    ;; close! on a live attachment reaches the host socket as a plain\n   224\t    ;; detachment with no close-failure diagnostic.\n   225\t    (let [fresh (fake-socket)\n   226\t          traffic-2 (buffer)\n   227\t          handle-2 (:dao.stream/handle (attach-with-fake traffic-2 fresh))]\n   228\t      (fire-text! fresh {:ws/frame :ws/accept})\n   229\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/close! handle-2))))\n   230\t      (is (= [1000 \"dao.stream/detached\"] (last @(:closes fresh)))))))\n   231\t\n   232\t\n   233\t;; A dao.stream.remote reflection over the wired boundary is proven\n   234\t;; portably (no host, no socket) in dao.stream.ws-project-test's own\n   235\t;; attachment-filtering and dial/reflection tests; nothing Node-specific\n   236\t;; remains to prove here once the wire is a channel rather than an RPC\n   237\t;; envelope.\n   238\t\n   239\t\n   240\t;; =============================================================================\n   241\t;; Async harness for the real-socket layer\n   242\t;; =============================================================================\n   243\t\n   244\t\n   245\t(defn- wait-for\n   246\t  \"Poll `pred` every 10ms until it returns truthy or `deadline-ms` passes.\n   247\t   The callback receives the value or nil, exactly once.\"\n   248\t  [pred deadline-ms cb]\n   249\t  (let [deadline (+ (.now js/Date) deadline-ms)]\n   250\t    (letfn [(poll\n   251\t              []\n   252\t              (let [v (try (pred) (catch :default _ nil))]\n   253\t                (cond\n   254\t                  v (cb v)\n   255\t                  (< deadline (.now js/Date)) (cb nil)\n   256\t                  :else (js/setTimeout poll 10))))]\n   257\t      (poll))))\n   258\t\n   259\t\n   260\t(defn- finish-once\n   261\t  [done]\n   262\t  (let [armed (atom true)]\n   263\t    (fn []\n   264\t      (when @armed\n   265\t        (reset! armed false)\n   266\t        (done)))))\n   267\t\n   268\t\n   269\t(defn- teardown!\n   270\t  [fixture clients & tickers]\n   271\t  (doseq [t tickers] (js/clearInterval t))\n   272\t  (doseq [c clients] (stream/close! (:handle c)))\n   273\t  (node/stop-listening! @(:listener fixture)))\n   274\t\n   275\t\n   276\t(defn- run-step\n   277\t  \"Invoke (step value) guarded so an unexpected throw still completes the\n   278\t   async test instead of hanging its ticker.\"\n   279\t  [finish step value]\n   280\t  (try\n   281\t    (step value)\n   282\t    (catch :default e\n   283\t      (is false (str \"unexpected error: \" e))\n   284\t      (finish))))\n   285\t\n   286\t\n   287\t(defn- after-bound\n   288\t  \"Invoke (step port) once the server reports its bound port -- `server-\n   289\t   fixture` already started listening.  A bind that never completes\n   290\t   fails, tears down, finishes.\"\n   291\t  [fixture ticker finish step]\n   292\t  (wait-for #(node/listener-port @(:listener fixture)) 2000\n   293\t            (fn [port]\n   294\t              (if (number? port)\n   295\t                (run-step finish step port)\n   296\t                (do (is false \"listener never reported a bound port\")\n   297\t                    (teardown! fixture [] ticker)\n   298\t                    (finish))))))\n   299\t\n   300\t\n   301\t(defn- after\n   302\t  \"Poll pred every 10ms until truthy or deadline, then invoke (step value).\n   303\t   A timeout fails with message, tears down, and finishes.\"\n   304\t  [deadline-ms pred message fixture ticker clients finish step]\n   305\t  (wait-for pred deadline-ms\n   306\t            (fn [value]\n   307\t              (if value\n   308\t                (run-step finish step value)\n   309\t                (do (is false message)\n   310\t                    (teardown! fixture clients ticker)\n   311\t                    (finish))))))\n   312\t\n   313\t\n   314\t;; =============================================================================\n   315\t;; The serving composition around a real Node listener\n   316\t;; =============================================================================\n   317\t\n   318\t\n   319\t(defn- server-fixture\n   320\t  \"Compose the full serving stack around a real Node listener.\n   321\t\n   322\t   Everything here is explicit test-owned state: media, cursors minted before\n   323\t   listener bind, a per-attachment traffic registry the medium factory fills,\n   324\t   a per-attachment RPC service registry the inbound interpreter fills, and\n   325\t   the listener the start policy retains.  The adapter owns none of it.\n   326\t\n   327\t   `:codecs` (an optional key of the map arity) selects the endpoint's codec\n   328\t   table and therefore the subprotocols its listener negotiates; the default\n   329\t   is the Transit-only table, exactly as before the dual-profile work.\n   330\t\n   700\t        (is (= :v1 (:dao.stream/value (ds/next refl c0)))\n   701\t            \"the reflection resolved and reads the served entry\")\n   702\t        (let [system (-> system (fact! (lease/renewal :l1)) (tick! 7) step!)]\n   703\t          (is (= {:ms 7} (get-in system [:judge :ledger :l1 :last-observation]))\n   704\t              \"the renewal on the per-author medium counted as evidence\")\n   705\t          (let [system (-> system (tick! 18) step!)]\n   706\t            (is (not (contains? @table \"served-1\"))\n   707\t                \"the idempotent reclaim removed the entry\")\n   708\t            (is (= [(lease/lapsed :l1 :silence)] (records system))\n   709\t                \"the :lapsed record is on the grantor's writer\")\n   710\t            (is (not (contains? (get-in system [:judge :ledger]) :l1))\n   711\t                \"the ledger no longer holds the lease\")\n   712\t            ;; one more reflection request and mirror step: the mirror\n   713\t            ;; answers not-found, the reflection becomes gone\n   714\t            (is (= :dao.stream/blocked (:dao.stream/outcome (ds/next refl c0))))\n   715\t            (serve!)\n   716\t            (let [ans (ds/next refl c0)]\n   717\t              (is (= :dao.stream/transport-error (:dao.stream/outcome ans)))\n   718\t              (is (= :dao.stream.remote/not-found\n   719\t                     (:dao.stream.remote/reason ans))))\n   720\t            (let [ans (ds/append! refl :x)]\n   721\t              (is (= :dao.stream/transport-error (:dao.stream/outcome ans)))\n   722\t              (is (= :dao.stream.remote/not-found\n   723\t                     (:dao.stream.remote/reason ans))\n   724\t                  \"a subsequent handle operation observes the same\n   725\t                   transport error\"))))))))\n   726\t\n   727\t\n   728\t(deftest shared-work-claim-sketch-test\n   729\t  (testing \"sketch: the shared-work claim -- a composition-supplied\n   730\t            reclaim following call-close!'s idempotency\"\n   731\t    ;; A shared-work claim's reclaim is a composition-supplied procedure\n   732\t    ;; in call-close!'s idempotency shape (serving.cljc:38-43): the first\n   733\t    ;; invocation performs the release and reports success; later\n   734\t    ;; invocations see the work already released and report success again\n   735\t    ;; without acting twice -- which is what the judge's pending-retry\n   736\t    ;; path demands of every reclaim it may invoke more than once.\n   737\t    (let [work (atom {:released? false})\n   738\t          releases (atom 0)\n   739\t          reclaim (fn [_subject]\n   740\t                    (when-not (:released? @work)\n   741\t                      (swap! work assoc :released? true)\n   742\t                      (swap! releases inc))\n   743\t                    true)\n   744\t          system (composed {:reclaim reclaim})\n   745\t          system (-> system\n   746\t                     (update :judge lease/author-grant\n   747\t                             (lease/grant :l1 :shared-work :holder-a {:ms 10}))\n   748\t                     (tick! 1)\n   749\t                     step!)\n   750\t          ;; the writer fails before the record, so the lease sits\n   751\t          ;; pending and the next pass invokes the procedure AGAIN\n   752\t          system (-> system\n   753\t                     (update :judge assoc :writer\n   754\t                             (fake-writer :dao.stream/full))\n   755\t                     (tick! 12)\n   756\t                     step!)\n   757\t          system (-> system\n   758\t                     (update :judge assoc :writer (:writer system))\n   759\t                     (tick! 13)\n   760\t                     step!)]\n   761\t      (is (= 1 @releases)\n   762\t          \"two reclaim invocations, one release: the procedure is idempotent\")\n   763\t      (is (true? (:released? @work)))\n   764\t      (is (= [(lease/lapsed :l1 :silence)] (records system))\n   765\t          \"the retry recorded after the writer recovered\"))))\n   766\t\n   767\t\n   768\t;; C5/C6/C7 are pinned outside the runtime tests, as the plan's §7 states:\n   769\t;; no timer or clock call exists in src/cljc/dao/lease.cljc (the grep),\n   770\t;; dao.lease requires dao.stream and never the reverse (by construction),\n   771\t;; and no machinery renews on a holder's behalf (the holder section has no\n   772\t;; renewal-appending function at all -- appending is the control flow's\n   773\t;; own act, recorded through observe-renewal).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
